1
00:00:16,015 --> 00:00:19,519
GWIMYEONAM ROCK

2
00:00:19,602 --> 00:00:24,232
2 HOURS PASSED
GWIMYEONAM ROCK

3
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:26,860
TODAY'S DESTINATION

4
00:00:26,943 --> 00:00:30,321
MORE THAN 2 HOURS LEFT
UNTIL THEY ARRIVE AT HUIUNGAK SHELTER

5
00:00:31,322 --> 00:00:33,283
Would you like an energy gel?

6
00:00:33,366 --> 00:00:35,702
Oh, I have sweet red bean jelly.

7
00:00:36,578 --> 00:00:37,996
-Do you want one?
-Yes, please.

8
00:00:38,913 --> 00:00:40,248
-I have a lot.
-Thank you.

9
00:00:40,331 --> 00:00:42,500
-I'll give you one too, Chae-min.
-Thank you.

10
00:00:43,084 --> 00:00:45,128
TRAIL FOOD CAN BE EATEN
WITHOUT COOKING WHILE HIKING

11
00:00:45,211 --> 00:00:46,838
It's my first time buying it too.

12
00:00:46,921 --> 00:00:47,797
Thank you.

13
00:00:47,881 --> 00:00:48,715
Sure.

14
00:00:49,716 --> 00:00:53,178
TRYING TRAIL FOOD FOR THE FIRST TIME

15
00:00:59,517 --> 00:01:00,685
It's tasty.

16
00:01:01,686 --> 00:01:04,397
<i>The jelly Car, the garden gave me halfway</i>

17
00:01:04,481 --> 00:01:05,648
<i>gave me a boost of energy.</i>

18
00:01:05,732 --> 00:01:08,151
When you hike,

19
00:01:08,234 --> 00:01:09,277
you tend to crave snacks

20
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:11,988
more than proper meals.

21
00:01:16,076 --> 00:01:16,910
This red bean jelly.

22
00:01:16,993 --> 00:01:18,953
The sugar… Gosh.

23
00:01:19,496 --> 00:01:20,789
It's so delicious.

24
00:01:22,749 --> 00:01:23,875
Gosh, the red bean jelly…

25
00:01:23,958 --> 00:01:24,959
Would you like a bite?

26
00:01:25,043 --> 00:01:26,044
No thanks.

27
00:01:26,127 --> 00:01:27,378
It's so good, though.

28
00:01:27,462 --> 00:01:29,172
-Can I…
-Sure, have a bite.

29
00:01:29,255 --> 00:01:30,799
It'll give you a sugar rush.

30
00:01:31,674 --> 00:01:33,134
That's it. This is insane.

31
00:01:35,595 --> 00:01:37,138
You should have this later too.

32
00:01:37,222 --> 00:01:38,097
-This…
-Yes.

33
00:01:38,932 --> 00:01:40,558
Whatever is easy to eat is the best.

34
00:01:40,642 --> 00:01:42,352
Even chewing will make you

35
00:01:42,435 --> 00:01:43,520
feel tired.

36
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:45,647
You get what I mean?

37
00:01:45,730 --> 00:01:47,440
Something that you can just swallow.

38
00:01:47,941 --> 00:01:49,025
Even chewing tires you out.

39
00:01:50,485 --> 00:01:51,694
Everyone looks

40
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:53,446
a lot less bloated compared to before.

41
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:59,035
You should ask him again now.

42
00:01:59,119 --> 00:02:00,703
I'm sure he's changed his mind.

43
00:02:01,746 --> 00:02:02,872
He doesn't look happy.

44
00:02:02,956 --> 00:02:03,832
Exactly.

45
00:02:04,332 --> 00:02:05,416
He'd have changed his mind.

46
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:07,418
"Darn it, who suggested this?"

47
00:02:10,588 --> 00:02:11,422
NAH YUNG-SUK, 51

48
00:02:11,506 --> 00:02:14,259
Producer Nah, come over.
Let's have a serious conversation.

49
00:02:14,968 --> 00:02:16,761
-You're regretting it.
-You're so fast.

50
00:02:17,762 --> 00:02:18,638
Aren't you tired?

51
00:02:18,721 --> 00:02:19,889
-I'm tired.
-They are.

52
00:02:19,973 --> 00:02:21,099
I'm hungry.

53
00:02:21,808 --> 00:02:22,642
I'm hungry.

54
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:25,770
GREEN OLD AGE

55
00:02:27,063 --> 00:02:29,440
Candy has never tasted this good.

56
00:02:30,984 --> 00:02:32,277
Red bean jelly is delicious.

57
00:02:33,027 --> 00:02:33,862
Red bean jelly…

58
00:02:34,696 --> 00:02:36,906
Imagine how good
pork belly would taste later.

59
00:02:36,990 --> 00:02:38,408
That would be insane.

60
00:02:38,491 --> 00:02:40,034
<i>Ramyeon</i> on top of that.

61
00:02:41,202 --> 00:02:42,579
2 WEEKS AGO

62
00:02:42,662 --> 00:02:43,955
I'd like to help in some way.

63
00:02:44,038 --> 00:02:45,415
I'll pack some <i>gimbap.</i>

64
00:02:45,498 --> 00:02:46,916
I'll bring <i>gimbap</i> and hand warmers.

65
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,084
DISCUSSING THE HIKE'S LUNCH

66
00:02:48,168 --> 00:02:50,378
Shall we grill some meat and boil <i>ramyeon?</i>

67
00:02:50,461 --> 00:02:52,755
LUNCH: PORK BELLY AND RAMYEON

68
00:02:52,839 --> 00:02:54,132
Then I'll buy meat.

69
00:02:54,215 --> 00:02:55,550
Buy the tasty parts.

70
00:02:55,633 --> 00:02:56,593
We can each buy half.

71
00:02:56,676 --> 00:02:57,969
Half each?

72
00:02:58,052 --> 00:02:59,679
I'll take the camping cookset.

73
00:03:00,555 --> 00:03:02,098
I don't eat a lot when I film.

74
00:03:02,181 --> 00:03:04,142
LUNCH PREP DECIDED IN NO TIME

75
00:03:04,225 --> 00:03:05,518
-Goodness.
-Goodness.

76
00:03:05,602 --> 00:03:06,769
GETTING READY TO HIKE AGAIN

77
00:03:06,853 --> 00:03:08,688
-Why does my bag…
-It suddenly feels heavy.

78
00:03:08,771 --> 00:03:10,982
-It gets heavier.
-Darn it.

79
00:03:12,567 --> 00:03:14,861
I couldn't explain earlier
because things were hectic,

80
00:03:15,361 --> 00:03:16,613
but that rock up there

81
00:03:16,696 --> 00:03:18,948
is called Gwimyeonam Rock.

82
00:03:19,449 --> 00:03:21,242
The name means it has the face of a ghost.

83
00:03:21,326 --> 00:03:22,577
THE DOCENT GOES AT IT AGAIN

84
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:25,371
Can you see the white part
of the left rock?

85
00:03:26,122 --> 00:03:27,373
-The white part?
-Yes.

86
00:03:27,457 --> 00:03:28,666
The white part.

87
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:31,252
Can you see the white part
of the left rock?

88
00:03:31,336 --> 00:03:32,170
MUNCHING

89
00:03:32,253 --> 00:03:34,464
-The white part?
-Yes. The white part.

90
00:03:35,173 --> 00:03:36,299
-Over there.
-On the left.

91
00:03:36,382 --> 00:03:38,551
Doesn't it look like a human face?
Does it not?

92
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:39,844
-It is that one.
-Hold on.

93
00:03:39,928 --> 00:03:41,304
Did you make this up?

94
00:03:42,472 --> 00:03:44,224
-I don't see it.
-Which part is white?

95
00:03:44,307 --> 00:03:45,266
On the left there.

96
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:46,935
Doesn't it look like a human face?

97
00:03:47,018 --> 00:03:48,186
IT'S UNCLEAR FROM DOWN HERE

98
00:03:48,269 --> 00:03:49,187
Like a Moai statue.

99
00:03:49,270 --> 00:03:52,941
IT WAS NAMED AS SUCH
BECAUSE IT RESEMBLES A GHOST'S FACE

100
00:03:53,024 --> 00:03:57,362
LEGEND HAS IT THAT A SAGE WAS MESMERIZED
BY THE VIEW OF CHEONBULDONGGYEGOK VALLEY

101
00:03:57,445 --> 00:04:00,823
AND APPOINTED GWIMYEONAM ROCK
AS THE GATEKEEPER OF THE VALLEY

102
00:04:00,907 --> 00:04:01,950
ORIGIN OF GWIMYEONAM ROCK

103
00:04:02,033 --> 00:04:03,451
HE DIDN'T MAKE IT UP

104
00:04:04,410 --> 00:04:06,996
2 HOURS 5 MINUTES PASSED
SET OFF FROM GWIMYEONAM ROCK

105
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:07,914
Goodness.

106
00:04:08,414 --> 00:04:09,791
What time is it?

107
00:04:09,874 --> 00:04:11,000
It's 9:00 a.m.

108
00:04:11,084 --> 00:04:12,502
Gosh, already?

109
00:04:13,086 --> 00:04:14,420
Time flies when you hike.

110
00:04:16,798 --> 00:04:20,551
HIGH-SPEED LOW-ENDURANCE GUY
TAKES THE LEAD AGAIN

111
00:04:20,635 --> 00:04:24,472
SPECIALTY: FLAT GROUND

112
00:04:24,555 --> 00:04:27,725
WEAKNESS: UPHILL

113
00:04:32,689 --> 00:04:36,109
HE CROSSES FLAT GROUND AT BREAKNECK SPEED

114
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:44,117
THE OTHERS WALK AT THEIR OWN SPEED

115
00:04:44,617 --> 00:04:47,161
HE RUNS INTO HIS WEAKNESS AGAIN

116
00:04:48,663 --> 00:04:50,999
1ST PERIOD: UPHILL STAIRS

117
00:04:52,583 --> 00:04:55,086
2ND PERIOD: UPHILL STAIRS

118
00:04:56,421 --> 00:04:58,840
3RD PERIOD: UPHILL STAIRS

119
00:05:00,341 --> 00:05:03,594
MAKE-UP CLASS: STAIRS

120
00:05:09,726 --> 00:05:11,644
This is really tough.

121
00:05:13,187 --> 00:05:15,732
HE TAKES A REST
AFTER PUSHING HIMSELF TOO HARD

122
00:05:15,815 --> 00:05:17,191
I didn't mean to,

123
00:05:17,859 --> 00:05:18,776
but I went too fast.

124
00:05:19,485 --> 00:05:20,403
I'm beat.

125
00:05:21,946 --> 00:05:23,156
We can hike together slowly.

126
00:05:23,239 --> 00:05:24,657
-Take it slow.
-Watch out.

127
00:05:24,741 --> 00:05:26,034
Don't mind those behind you.

128
00:05:26,534 --> 00:05:28,036
Take it slow at your own pace.

129
00:05:28,911 --> 00:05:31,080
TARZZAN TAKES THE LEAD THIS TIME

130
00:05:31,664 --> 00:05:34,000
MIDDLE 1: DOWOON

131
00:05:34,083 --> 00:05:37,003
MIDDLE 2: CAR, THE GARDEN

132
00:05:37,587 --> 00:05:38,421
This is hard.

133
00:05:38,504 --> 00:05:39,630
BACK: CHAE-MIN

134
00:05:40,673 --> 00:05:47,680
THE 2ND LINEUP OF THE SEORAKSAN HIKE

135
00:05:56,606 --> 00:05:57,565
Look at the view.

136
00:05:57,648 --> 00:05:59,358
Right, it sure is pretty.

137
00:06:01,277 --> 00:06:02,195
It's amazing.

138
00:06:02,695 --> 00:06:04,822
But there's no end to the stairs.

139
00:06:05,406 --> 00:06:07,992
Why are there so many stairs?

140
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:12,163
SEORAKSAN NATIONAL PARK TRAIL

141
00:06:12,246 --> 00:06:17,418
THE TRAIL GUIDE ADVISES HIKERS TO CHECK
THEIR PHYSICAL HEALTH BEFORE CLIMBING,

142
00:06:17,502 --> 00:06:21,881
AS THE STAIRS CONTINUE
THROUGHOUT THE TRAIL

143
00:06:24,509 --> 00:06:27,804
AN EXAMPLE OF "NOT FIT ENOUGH TO CLIMB"

144
00:06:29,472 --> 00:06:32,600
AN EXAMPLE OF "FIT ENOUGH TO CLIMB"

145
00:06:35,228 --> 00:06:36,145
I'm tired.

146
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:39,440
SIGHS

147
00:06:41,526 --> 00:06:46,197
CAR, NOT GOING
HAS SLOWED DOWN SIGNIFICANTLY

148
00:06:46,781 --> 00:06:48,074
CHAE-MIN FORCES A LAUGH

149
00:06:48,616 --> 00:06:50,118
I should really walk. I…

150
00:06:50,618 --> 00:06:51,786
I should just walk.

151
00:06:53,079 --> 00:06:54,205
I'll walk calmly.

152
00:06:54,288 --> 00:06:55,915
Are you sure you're a fast walker?

153
00:06:57,291 --> 00:06:58,167
I have no energy.

154
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:03,297
THE VANGUARD WALKS ACROSS

155
00:07:03,381 --> 00:07:06,092
TARZZAN, DOWOON

156
00:07:07,385 --> 00:07:08,761
A CAMERAMAN

157
00:07:09,637 --> 00:07:12,348
THEY APPEAR MUCH LATER

158
00:07:12,431 --> 00:07:14,684
CAR, THE GARDEN, CHAE-MIN

159
00:07:15,393 --> 00:07:16,894
Are you okay?

160
00:07:16,978 --> 00:07:17,854
What?

161
00:07:18,354 --> 00:07:19,480
You suddenly…

162
00:07:19,564 --> 00:07:21,774
You suddenly look ill.

163
00:07:22,733 --> 00:07:24,152
You look pale.

164
00:07:24,819 --> 00:07:26,070
Where's Producer Nah?

165
00:07:26,946 --> 00:07:28,865
-I'll talk to him now.
-He's at the back.

166
00:07:29,365 --> 00:07:30,700
I'll tell him now.

167
00:07:30,783 --> 00:07:32,201
HE'S READY TO QUIT THE SHOW

168
00:07:33,035 --> 00:07:34,454
We really need to take it slow.

169
00:07:34,537 --> 00:07:36,038
-We shouldn't show off.
-That's true.

170
00:07:36,122 --> 00:07:37,832
The moral of hiking is not to show off.

171
00:07:37,915 --> 00:07:38,916
SAID BY CAR, THE GARDEN

172
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:39,834
Seriously…

173
00:07:39,917 --> 00:07:42,503
TAKING A MOMENT TO CHECK THE MICS

174
00:07:45,006 --> 00:07:46,883
KIM SEON-U, AUDIO DIRECTOR

175
00:07:46,966 --> 00:07:47,884
Are you all right?

176
00:07:48,384 --> 00:07:49,385
My gosh.

177
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:51,345
This could break your back.

178
00:07:51,429 --> 00:07:53,347
This is madness.

179
00:07:53,431 --> 00:07:54,432
What is?

180
00:07:54,515 --> 00:07:55,975
Try carrying this.

181
00:07:57,226 --> 00:07:58,060
What?

182
00:07:59,770 --> 00:08:00,771
How heavy is it?

183
00:08:01,272 --> 00:08:02,106
Try it.

184
00:08:02,190 --> 00:08:04,734
ABOUT 25 KG

185
00:08:04,817 --> 00:08:05,651
I'm sorry.

186
00:08:05,735 --> 00:08:07,653
Why do you have so many things inside?

187
00:08:07,737 --> 00:08:08,988
I think it's the equipment.

188
00:08:09,071 --> 00:08:10,948
He brought an audio mixer.

189
00:08:11,032 --> 00:08:13,618
The directors must've hated it
when they heard of this show.

190
00:08:13,701 --> 00:08:15,286
CAMERAMAN LAUGHING

191
00:08:15,953 --> 00:08:17,413
This might freeze later.

192
00:08:17,497 --> 00:08:18,789
-I think it will.
-Your mustache.

193
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:20,124
Thank you.

194
00:08:22,043 --> 00:08:23,294
An icicle formed on it.

195
00:08:23,377 --> 00:08:24,837
AN ICICLE FORMED ON HIS MUSTACHE

196
00:08:26,047 --> 00:08:27,340
It must be really tough.

197
00:08:27,423 --> 00:08:28,466
Gosh, the mixer…

198
00:08:29,091 --> 00:08:31,427
If we walk a bit more,
there's a very long staircase

199
00:08:31,511 --> 00:08:33,471
called Oryeonpokpo Falls.

200
00:08:33,971 --> 00:08:35,306
We just need to pass that…

201
00:08:35,389 --> 00:08:36,224
ALLERGIC TO DOCENTS

202
00:08:36,307 --> 00:08:37,683
…and reach the first shelter.

203
00:08:37,767 --> 00:08:39,393
Is that the second crux?

204
00:08:39,477 --> 00:08:40,603
More or less.

205
00:08:40,686 --> 00:08:41,938
-Let's go.
-Okay.

206
00:08:42,021 --> 00:08:43,439
SET OFF AFTER MIC CHECKS

207
00:08:43,523 --> 00:08:45,483
I'll walk very slowly, Chae-min.

208
00:08:45,566 --> 00:08:46,859
Yes, take it slow.

209
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:48,945
DOWOON LEADS NOW

210
00:08:49,028 --> 00:08:50,446
You somehow feel the urge

211
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:53,574
to walk fast when you take the lead.

212
00:08:56,244 --> 00:08:59,121
THE 3RD LINEUP OF THE SEORAKSAN HIKE

213
00:09:00,915 --> 00:09:03,793
HE WALKS LEISURELY

214
00:09:05,503 --> 00:09:08,714
HE EVEN HAS HIS HANDS BEHIND HIS BACK

215
00:09:08,798 --> 00:09:10,049
Q. WHY DO YOU WALK THAT WAY?

216
00:09:10,132 --> 00:09:11,717
-Your hands behind your back.
-Right.

217
00:09:11,801 --> 00:09:12,635
That's because

218
00:09:12,718 --> 00:09:15,096
I tend to walk using my pelvis.

219
00:09:15,179 --> 00:09:17,181
I wasn't trying to show off or anything.

220
00:09:17,265 --> 00:09:19,934
I do this and bend slightly forward

221
00:09:20,017 --> 00:09:21,852
to feel the movements of my pelvis.

222
00:09:23,479 --> 00:09:27,775
WALKING AND FEELING THE STIMULATION
ON HIS HIP JOINTS

223
00:09:27,858 --> 00:09:30,069
Q. HOW DO YOU WALK WHEN IT'S STEEP?

224
00:09:30,152 --> 00:09:31,320
When it's steep, right.

225
00:09:31,404 --> 00:09:33,656
-You used the poles.
-Yes, I make them shorter.

226
00:09:33,739 --> 00:09:35,950
I make them shorter
and use them like canes.

227
00:09:36,033 --> 00:09:37,368
IT IS RECOMMENDED TO HOLD

228
00:09:37,451 --> 00:09:38,911
THE POLES 5 TO 10 CM SHORTER UPHILL

229
00:09:38,995 --> 00:09:40,997
A lot of hikers recommend that.

230
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:42,832
You just figured it out yourself?

231
00:09:42,915 --> 00:09:43,958
To survive.

232
00:09:44,458 --> 00:09:46,002
I kept discovering stuff to survive.

233
00:09:46,085 --> 00:09:47,712
"At this rate, I really might die."

234
00:09:47,795 --> 00:09:48,629
You yourself…

235
00:09:49,255 --> 00:09:50,089
That's right.

236
00:09:50,172 --> 00:09:52,842
What you see on the left
is Oryeonpokpo Falls.

237
00:09:52,925 --> 00:09:53,801
Yes.

238
00:09:56,429 --> 00:09:58,014
Car-the will faint when he sees that.

239
00:10:00,433 --> 00:10:02,560
ORYEONPOKPO FALLS

240
00:10:02,643 --> 00:10:05,104
5 SMALL WATERFALLS CASCADE

241
00:10:05,187 --> 00:10:08,399
THROUGH A STEEP ROCKY VALLEY

242
00:10:08,482 --> 00:10:11,736
IT IS KNOWN TO HAVE THE BEST VIEW
IN CHEONBULDONGGYEGOK VALLEY

243
00:10:13,029 --> 00:10:14,572
Is that the staircase?

244
00:10:16,407 --> 00:10:19,910
AN ENDLESS STAIRCASE TRAIL
THAT WINDS ALONGSIDE THE WATERFALL

245
00:10:22,872 --> 00:10:26,626
THE 2ND CRUX SELECTED BY THE STAFF

246
00:10:27,209 --> 00:10:30,046
ONCE YOU WALK UP
THE SEEMINGLY NEVER-ENDING STAIRS,

247
00:10:30,963 --> 00:10:34,008
YOU ARRIVE AT THE FIRST SHELTER!

248
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:41,057
WILL THEY BE ABLE TO OVERCOME
THE SECOND CRUX?

249
00:10:46,687 --> 00:10:49,106
Once we climb up the stairs,
we'll get to the shelter.

250
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:50,775
I see, will we eat there?

251
00:10:50,858 --> 00:10:51,692
No.

252
00:10:51,776 --> 00:10:53,569
We could eat something simple there.

253
00:10:53,653 --> 00:10:54,904
We can have <i>gimbap.</i>

254
00:10:54,987 --> 00:10:57,073
<i>-Gimbap.</i>
-I feel really hungry again.

255
00:10:57,156 --> 00:10:59,700
I'm more hungry than exhausted.

256
00:10:59,784 --> 00:11:00,868
-Yes.
-Me too.

257
00:11:00,951 --> 00:11:02,036
-Really?
-Yes.

258
00:11:03,162 --> 00:11:04,955
I have no energy because I'm hungry.

259
00:11:06,165 --> 00:11:07,541
Let's just walk.

260
00:11:07,625 --> 00:11:08,459
Okay.

261
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:11,837
When you think about it,
there's no need to go fast.

262
00:11:11,921 --> 00:11:12,755
That's right.

263
00:11:12,838 --> 00:11:14,674
They can't film anything without us.

264
00:11:15,174 --> 00:11:16,008
You're right.

265
00:11:16,509 --> 00:11:18,719
Let's walk as slow as we can.

266
00:11:18,803 --> 00:11:20,888
And we won't be able to arrive in time.

267
00:11:20,971 --> 00:11:22,765
-So we'll descend midway.
-Quit halfway.

268
00:11:22,848 --> 00:11:24,058
-That doesn't sound bad.
-Yes.

269
00:11:24,683 --> 00:11:26,644
We're walking…

270
00:11:26,727 --> 00:11:28,187
Almost in slow motion.

271
00:11:30,064 --> 00:11:32,608
I thought we'd come far,
but we're not even halfway there.

272
00:11:37,488 --> 00:11:38,864
It sure is pretty, though.

273
00:11:38,948 --> 00:11:40,616
The snow is falling so beautifully.

274
00:11:41,492 --> 00:11:42,326
It's pretty.

275
00:11:44,745 --> 00:11:48,457
IT STARTS TO SNOW ON SEORAKSAN

276
00:11:48,541 --> 00:11:52,420
CURRENT TEMPERATURE: -11.4℃
WIND CHILL: -24.3℃

277
00:11:55,464 --> 00:12:00,469
WEST WIND BLOWING AT 15.1 M/S

278
00:12:08,310 --> 00:12:09,145
Look at the snow.

279
00:12:09,228 --> 00:12:10,938
-The wind is blowing.
-Gosh.

280
00:12:14,525 --> 00:12:15,609
Oh no, your hat!

281
00:12:15,693 --> 00:12:16,527
No!

282
00:12:18,821 --> 00:12:22,241
TARZZAN'S HAT ESCAPES

283
00:12:22,324 --> 00:12:23,242
Did his hat fly away?

284
00:12:23,325 --> 00:12:24,452
It flew away.

285
00:12:24,535 --> 00:12:26,412
-Really?
-The hat.

286
00:12:26,495 --> 00:12:27,329
HE LOSES HIS HAT

287
00:12:27,413 --> 00:12:28,372
No way.

288
00:12:28,998 --> 00:12:30,249
You need to let it go.

289
00:12:31,167 --> 00:12:33,377
-Let it go.
-You should just let it go.

290
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:37,131
Farewell.

291
00:12:37,214 --> 00:12:39,383
The wind was pretty bad just now.

292
00:12:39,467 --> 00:12:40,301
This isn't easy.

293
00:12:44,889 --> 00:12:45,806
Here, wear this.

294
00:12:46,974 --> 00:12:47,808
Use this for now.

295
00:12:47,892 --> 00:12:49,477
I'm worried it might fly away again.

296
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:51,145
-It has Velcro.
-Fasten it under.

297
00:12:51,228 --> 00:12:52,563
It has Velcro.

298
00:12:53,856 --> 00:12:55,191
I earned a lot of brownie points.

299
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:58,527
You're part of ALLDAY PROJECT now.

300
00:12:58,611 --> 00:12:59,778
You're an ambassador.

301
00:13:01,655 --> 00:13:03,073
That gave us a chance to rest.

302
00:13:03,157 --> 00:13:03,991
Yes.

303
00:13:08,078 --> 00:13:14,168
STILL WALKING SLOWLY

304
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:19,298
You were really fast just now.

305
00:13:19,798 --> 00:13:20,633
I overdid it.

306
00:13:20,716 --> 00:13:23,594
I thought you were a really good hiker.

307
00:13:23,677 --> 00:13:24,762
That was me being stupid.

308
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:41,487
Going up isn't the issue.

309
00:13:41,570 --> 00:13:44,573
Having to go down this route again…

310
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:46,158
Is there only one path?

311
00:13:53,749 --> 00:13:57,002
Once you reach the end of the staircase,
you'll arrive at the shelter.

312
00:13:57,086 --> 00:13:57,920
-Okay.
-Okay.

313
00:14:05,719 --> 00:14:06,554
My gosh.

314
00:14:07,471 --> 00:14:08,597
We've reached the restrooms.

315
00:14:09,306 --> 00:14:10,140
Gosh.

316
00:14:12,142 --> 00:14:15,896
THE FIRST SHELTER FINALLY REVEALS ITSELF

317
00:14:22,236 --> 00:14:24,738
How did they build this
all the way up here?

318
00:14:25,239 --> 00:14:26,824
That's really amazing.

319
00:14:26,907 --> 00:14:27,741
Exactly.

320
00:14:28,993 --> 00:14:31,954
2 HOURS 55 MINUTES PASSED

321
00:14:32,037 --> 00:14:35,666
ARRIVED AT THE FIRST SHELTER

322
00:14:35,749 --> 00:14:39,128
WHAT IS A SHELTER?

323
00:14:39,837 --> 00:14:44,174
A REST AREA WHERE YOU CAN REST WHILE
BEING SHELTERED FROM THE HARSH WEATHER

324
00:14:45,968 --> 00:14:47,803
THE STORE TO REPLENISH SUPPLIES

325
00:14:50,097 --> 00:14:52,099
A COZY STAY TO RECHARGE FOR THE NEXT DAY

326
00:14:52,975 --> 00:14:56,020
IT'S LIKE AN OASIS FOR HIKERS

327
00:14:56,103 --> 00:14:57,021
SEORAKSAN SOGONGWON

328
00:14:57,104 --> 00:14:58,314
BISEONDAE, GWIMYEONAM ROCK

329
00:14:58,397 --> 00:15:00,107
FOLLOWING CHEONBULDONGGYEGOK VALLEY

330
00:15:00,190 --> 00:15:02,818
YANGPOK SHELTER

331
00:15:05,696 --> 00:15:08,574
THEY DECIDE TO HAVE
A SHORT MAINTENANCE SESSION

332
00:15:09,491 --> 00:15:11,118
The water's frozen.

333
00:15:12,453 --> 00:15:13,746
You're right.

334
00:15:13,829 --> 00:15:14,663
It's frozen.

335
00:15:14,747 --> 00:15:16,206
THE WATER FROZE WHILE HIKING

336
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:17,583
It became a slushie.

337
00:15:22,087 --> 00:15:25,841
IT'S AS COLD AS A FREEZER

338
00:15:26,550 --> 00:15:28,135
Chae-min, do you want <i>gimbap</i> now?

339
00:15:28,218 --> 00:15:29,053
Shall we have a bit?

340
00:15:29,136 --> 00:15:30,095
-Do you want it?
-Yes.

341
00:15:30,679 --> 00:15:32,723
THE GIMBAP HE BROUGHT FROM SEOUL

342
00:15:33,599 --> 00:15:34,808
DOWOON LAUGHING

343
00:15:35,309 --> 00:15:37,102
EXCITED

344
00:15:37,853 --> 00:15:38,687
This is yours.

345
00:15:38,771 --> 00:15:39,730
Thank you.

346
00:15:40,439 --> 00:15:41,273
I like this <i>gimbap.</i>

347
00:15:41,357 --> 00:15:42,358
A SPEEDY DELIVERY

348
00:15:42,942 --> 00:15:44,026
Car, would you like <i>gimbap?</i>

349
00:15:44,109 --> 00:15:45,778
-Shall I have some?
-Sure, here.

350
00:15:46,278 --> 00:15:47,863
Thank you.

351
00:15:48,405 --> 00:15:49,365
Thank you.

352
00:15:49,865 --> 00:15:52,534
TAKING A BIG BITE

353
00:15:53,369 --> 00:15:56,497
CAR, THE GARDEN EATS IT WITHOUT ANY DELAY

354
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:02,920
Dowoon, thank you. It's delicious.

355
00:16:03,712 --> 00:16:05,172
FEELING PROUD

356
00:16:05,255 --> 00:16:07,049
Cold <i>gimbap</i>

357
00:16:07,132 --> 00:16:08,175
has its charms.

358
00:16:08,676 --> 00:16:09,969
COLD GIMBAP IS A DELICACY HERE

359
00:16:10,761 --> 00:16:13,138
TARZZAN JOINS THEM

360
00:16:14,598 --> 00:16:15,432
AMAZED

361
00:16:15,933 --> 00:16:16,767
It's good, right?

362
00:16:16,850 --> 00:16:18,435
It's so good.

363
00:16:18,519 --> 00:16:19,770
It's very cold but good.

364
00:16:22,189 --> 00:16:23,983
I smell <i>ramyeon.</i>

365
00:16:24,066 --> 00:16:25,359
They must be making some inside.

366
00:16:25,442 --> 00:16:27,653
EVERYONE GETS EXCITED
AT THE FAMILIAR SMELL

367
00:16:27,736 --> 00:16:29,488
It smells so good.

368
00:16:29,571 --> 00:16:30,489
The smell of <i>ramyeon.</i>

369
00:16:30,572 --> 00:16:31,740
It smells insane.

370
00:16:31,824 --> 00:16:32,825
Who is…

371
00:16:32,908 --> 00:16:34,493
Are they one of our crew?

372
00:16:37,955 --> 00:16:43,002
OTHER HIKERS ARE COOKING RAMYEON

373
00:16:43,085 --> 00:16:44,461
The smell is so…

374
00:16:45,504 --> 00:16:47,256
HE WALKS TOWARD THE RAMYEON
AS IF ENCHANTED

375
00:16:47,339 --> 00:16:49,967
We went up Gongnyong Ridge,
came back down,

376
00:16:50,050 --> 00:16:51,552
and then came back up here to eat.

377
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:55,764
<i>Remember the guys</i>
<i>who were eating</i> ramyeon <i>there?</i>

378
00:16:55,848 --> 00:16:58,559
<i>I was enticed by it,</i>
<i>and it was hard to bear.</i>

379
00:16:59,309 --> 00:17:00,352
I was very hungry.

380
00:17:00,436 --> 00:17:02,479
Hiking uphill is…

381
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:04,356
I looked it up on the Internet.

382
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:06,608
It says you burn around
300 to 500 calories per hour.

383
00:17:06,692 --> 00:17:07,860
VARIES ON WEIGHT AND INCLINE

384
00:17:07,943 --> 00:17:08,944
Well…

385
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:11,447
If I'd burned that many calories,

386
00:17:11,530 --> 00:17:12,781
I should've eaten something.

387
00:17:12,865 --> 00:17:13,866
BURNED 1,500 KCAL AT MAX

388
00:17:14,450 --> 00:17:15,409
Good luck.

389
00:17:15,909 --> 00:17:17,077
Thank you.

390
00:17:17,161 --> 00:17:18,787
-The smell…
-The smell.

391
00:17:18,871 --> 00:17:20,581
It's killing me.

392
00:17:20,664 --> 00:17:21,665
CHAE-MIN IS SUFFERING

393
00:17:22,666 --> 00:17:23,792
It smells so good.

394
00:17:24,626 --> 00:17:26,378
Eating <i>ramyeon</i> up there
would taste amazing.

395
00:17:26,462 --> 00:17:27,588
It smells so…

396
00:17:27,671 --> 00:17:28,756
I must have it soon.

397
00:17:29,923 --> 00:17:31,258
I brought the cookset.

398
00:17:31,842 --> 00:17:32,676
Nice.

399
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:33,969
QUICKLY GETS READY TO HIKE

400
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:35,763
Everyone.

401
00:17:35,846 --> 00:17:38,140
-The difficulty starts now.
-It was average until here.

402
00:17:38,223 --> 00:17:39,725
THEY'LL ENTER "HARD" MODE NOW

403
00:17:39,808 --> 00:17:42,603
Hearing that makes me

404
00:17:42,686 --> 00:17:43,729
so pissed.

405
00:17:44,688 --> 00:17:46,648
Saying it was average until now.

406
00:17:47,357 --> 00:17:48,525
So,

407
00:17:48,609 --> 00:17:50,069
who should I be mad at?

408
00:17:50,569 --> 00:17:51,862
At myself.

409
00:17:52,362 --> 00:17:54,656
SEETHING FOR NO CLEAR REASON

410
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:55,949
Gosh.

411
00:17:56,658 --> 00:17:57,785
This smell is torture.

412
00:17:57,868 --> 00:17:59,745
We must do our best for pork belly.

413
00:17:59,828 --> 00:18:01,830
-This smell is dangerous.
-This smell is dangerous.

414
00:18:01,914 --> 00:18:02,998
THE SMELL MOTIVATES THEM

415
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:05,125
That's motivating me a lot.

416
00:18:05,209 --> 00:18:06,460
Let's quickly go up.

417
00:18:06,543 --> 00:18:08,128
THEIR HUNGER DRIVES THEM TO MOVE FAST

418
00:18:08,212 --> 00:18:09,129
I'm hungry.

419
00:18:10,756 --> 00:18:13,550
2 KM LEFT UNTIL THEIR FINAL DESTINATION

420
00:18:14,134 --> 00:18:14,968
It's nice.

421
00:18:15,052 --> 00:18:17,221
3 HOURS 15 MINUTES PASSED
SET OFF FROM YANGPOK SHELTER

422
00:18:17,805 --> 00:18:19,556
After taking a rest and eating,

423
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:21,225
I feel like I'm back to my normal self.

424
00:18:21,308 --> 00:18:22,142
Yes, it's better.

425
00:18:22,684 --> 00:18:26,688
"EATING TRAIL FOOD GIVES YOU ENERGY"
-HIKING EXPERT PARK MIN-GU

426
00:18:28,273 --> 00:18:34,988
NOW THAT HE'S RECHARGED,
THE FAST WALKER STARTS TO SPEED BACK UP

427
00:18:35,072 --> 00:18:36,323
Right, I should walk slow.

428
00:18:37,407 --> 00:18:38,659
No fooling around.

429
00:18:41,537 --> 00:18:45,040
"DON'T SHOW OFF WHILE HIKING"
-CAR, THE GARDEN 30 MINUTES AGO

430
00:18:45,916 --> 00:18:50,129
AS EXPECTED OF THE EXPERT-LEVEL COURSE,
THE PATH IS VERY STEEP FROM THE START

431
00:18:52,506 --> 00:18:57,302
THEY ENTER THE STAIRCASE HELL

432
00:19:02,432 --> 00:19:09,022
THE STAIRCASE HELL SHOWS NO MERCY

433
00:19:09,648 --> 00:19:11,567
GROANS

434
00:19:11,650 --> 00:19:12,651
My thighs.

435
00:19:17,447 --> 00:19:19,366
CONGESTION

436
00:19:19,449 --> 00:19:20,742
-Are you okay?
-Yes.

437
00:19:21,827 --> 00:19:24,872
It might be better for you
to stay in Yangpok Shelter.

438
00:19:24,955 --> 00:19:26,582
If you force yourself…

439
00:19:26,665 --> 00:19:28,208
The next two hours will be tough.

440
00:19:30,627 --> 00:19:31,712
He's not feeling well.

441
00:19:31,795 --> 00:19:32,713
Who?

442
00:19:32,796 --> 00:19:33,755
The photographer.

443
00:19:36,550 --> 00:19:37,551
I got a slight cramp.

444
00:19:37,634 --> 00:19:38,969
THE PHOTOGRAPHER HAS A LEG CRAMP

445
00:19:39,052 --> 00:19:40,387
Then we'll go first.

446
00:19:40,470 --> 00:19:41,555
-Okay.
-Director, let's go.

447
00:19:42,055 --> 00:19:43,557
The rescue crew joined us.

448
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:46,810
THE SHOW WAS SHOT WITH THE COOPERATION
AND SUPPORT OF THE MOUNTAIN RESCUE TEAM

449
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:49,521
THE FIELD PHOTOGRAPHER GOES BACK

450
00:19:49,605 --> 00:19:51,064
TO THE SHELTER WITH THE RESCUE TEAM

451
00:19:52,482 --> 00:19:57,404
"ONE DOESN'T HAVE TO REACH THE SUMMIT"
-VOYTEK KURTYKA

452
00:19:58,238 --> 00:20:00,407
TAKING SLOW, SAFE STEPS

453
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:06,330
"IF YOU GO SLOW, YOU'RE INVINCIBLE"
FROM "HIKE SHELF" BY YOON SEONG-JUNG

454
00:20:07,122 --> 00:20:08,457
That's all stairs.

455
00:20:09,291 --> 00:20:13,170
MORE STAIRS

456
00:20:14,171 --> 00:20:16,715
DEJECTED

457
00:20:16,798 --> 00:20:18,133
Guys.

458
00:20:18,926 --> 00:20:20,802
This is Cheondangpokpo Falls.

459
00:20:20,886 --> 00:20:21,720
SICK OF HIM

460
00:20:21,803 --> 00:20:24,306
-What falls?
-Cheondangpokpo Falls.

461
00:20:24,806 --> 00:20:26,516
Does it take me to heaven?

462
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:30,270
More like this place makes you
feel like you're in heaven.

463
00:20:30,979 --> 00:20:31,813
IN HEAVEN

464
00:20:31,897 --> 00:20:33,523
That's how the legend goes.

465
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:34,942
And I wondered why he stopped us.

466
00:20:37,945 --> 00:20:40,530
I'm basically walking like this.

467
00:20:41,490 --> 00:20:42,658
And suddenly, he stops.

468
00:20:42,741 --> 00:20:43,742
"Why did you stop?"

469
00:20:43,825 --> 00:20:44,993
"Now, look at this."

470
00:20:47,996 --> 00:20:50,040
We just need to keep walking.

471
00:20:50,123 --> 00:20:50,999
So…

472
00:20:51,750 --> 00:20:53,335
You didn't make this up.

473
00:20:53,418 --> 00:20:54,294
Not at all.

474
00:20:55,128 --> 00:20:57,756
It's officially Cheondangpokpo Falls
of the National Park.

475
00:20:57,839 --> 00:21:00,592
THE LAST WATERFALL
IN CHEONBULDONGGYEGOK VALLEY

476
00:21:00,676 --> 00:21:04,429
CALLED "CHEONDANGPOKPO FALLS"
BECAUSE AFTER ENDURING HARDSHIPS

477
00:21:04,513 --> 00:21:08,767
IN THE MORTAL WORLD,
ARRIVING HERE FEELS LIKE HEAVEN

478
00:21:08,850 --> 00:21:10,310
But it's too cold.

479
00:21:10,394 --> 00:21:12,396
-It's completely frozen.
-That's hell.

480
00:21:14,022 --> 00:21:18,193
THOUGH IT'S HARD TO SEE
ITS TRUE BEAUTY IN WINTER,

481
00:21:21,029 --> 00:21:25,575
IT TRULY SHINES ON CLEAR DAYS

482
00:21:26,493 --> 00:21:28,245
Will it get hard for the next two hours?

483
00:21:28,328 --> 00:21:29,162
It'll be hard.

484
00:21:29,246 --> 00:21:30,580
This is a stairway to heaven.

485
00:21:30,664 --> 00:21:31,665
Not Cheondangpokpo Falls.

486
00:21:32,624 --> 00:21:33,625
Look at that.

487
00:21:33,709 --> 00:21:34,751
My gosh.

488
00:21:34,835 --> 00:21:35,711
That's crazy.

489
00:21:36,753 --> 00:21:43,760
A VERY STEEP STAIRCASE
NEXT TO CHEONDANGPOKPO FALLS

490
00:21:46,596 --> 00:21:47,514
This is too much.

491
00:21:50,183 --> 00:21:53,562
THE STAIRS BECOME STEEPER

492
00:21:55,397 --> 00:22:00,861
IT LOOKS EVEN SCARIER FROM BELOW

493
00:22:01,862 --> 00:22:05,282
SO STEEP THAT YOU CAN ONLY SEE
THE TOP OF THE HEAD OF THE PERSON BEHIND

494
00:22:05,365 --> 00:22:09,077
THEY JUST CAN'T SPEED UP

495
00:22:09,995 --> 00:22:12,205
TO MAKE IT WORSE, THE SMOOTH STAIRS

496
00:22:13,832 --> 00:22:17,002
BECOME COVERED IN SNOW

497
00:22:17,919 --> 00:22:20,964
AS THEY CLIMB HIGHER

498
00:22:21,048 --> 00:22:25,761
THEY'RE CLIMBING EVEN SLOWER

499
00:22:28,847 --> 00:22:31,641
THE SNOWY STAIRS HAVE A LONG WAY TO GO

500
00:22:33,852 --> 00:22:37,773
IT MAKES MATTERS WORSE

501
00:22:39,900 --> 00:22:43,528
WALKING MASTER BRINGS HIS HANDS FORWARD

502
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:48,408
HE CHANGES HIS WAY OF WALKING

503
00:22:49,409 --> 00:22:52,871
HE CRAWLS ON ALL FOURS

504
00:22:52,954 --> 00:22:55,916
<i>Which part was the hardest when going up?</i>

505
00:22:55,999 --> 00:22:57,209
The stairs.

506
00:22:57,292 --> 00:23:00,962
The metal stairs and the wooden stairs.

507
00:23:01,046 --> 00:23:04,174
Each step was high,
which made it difficult.

508
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:10,555
UNEXPECTEDLY, DOWOON IS HAVING A HARD TIME

509
00:23:17,104 --> 00:23:20,732
MEANWHILE, CAR, THE GARDEN
IS UNEXPECTEDLY DOING FINE

510
00:23:21,691 --> 00:23:22,526
Okay.

511
00:23:24,027 --> 00:23:25,737
<i>Stairs are better, actually.</i>

512
00:23:25,821 --> 00:23:26,780
<i>They're hard too,</i>

513
00:23:26,863 --> 00:23:29,407
but they have a fixed way of climbing.

514
00:23:29,908 --> 00:23:31,535
You just need to go like this.

515
00:23:32,119 --> 00:23:33,620
Stairs are fine.

516
00:23:34,162 --> 00:23:36,289
But for the paths with rocks and so on,

517
00:23:36,373 --> 00:23:37,958
where do I need to step?

518
00:23:38,917 --> 00:23:40,919
It's rather frustrating.

519
00:23:45,048 --> 00:23:51,680
ANOTHER DIFFICULT TRAIL FOLLOWS

520
