606
00:28:49,561 --> 00:28:54,441
CAR, THE GARDEN STAYS IN THE LEAD

607
00:28:56,234 --> 00:28:57,193
GROANS

608
00:28:57,277 --> 00:28:58,611
GROANS

609
00:28:58,695 --> 00:28:59,738
Seriously though,

610
00:29:00,238 --> 00:29:01,448
my thighs hurt so much.

611
00:29:02,157 --> 00:29:03,450
Let's take a rest, then.

612
00:29:04,284 --> 00:29:05,452
This is madness.

613
00:29:07,287 --> 00:29:08,538
Take it slow.

614
00:29:09,539 --> 00:29:10,707
You can crawl too.

615
00:29:11,624 --> 00:29:14,711
It must be tough
for those at the back too, anyway.

616
00:29:16,171 --> 00:29:17,005
GROANS

617
00:29:23,636 --> 00:29:24,929
<i>In the midst of that,</i>

618
00:29:25,013 --> 00:29:27,182
I felt the pain here.

619
00:29:29,058 --> 00:29:30,101
It hurt so bad.

620
00:29:31,019 --> 00:29:32,228
It really hurt.

621
00:29:32,312 --> 00:29:33,521
It really hurt here.

622
00:29:36,483 --> 00:29:39,277
HIS LEGS SWAY HELPLESSLY

623
00:29:49,871 --> 00:29:51,831
Guys, just another 30 minutes,
and you're there.

624
00:29:51,915 --> 00:29:52,832
Really?

625
00:29:52,916 --> 00:29:54,459
-Thirty minutes.
-Let's eat!

626
00:29:54,542 --> 00:29:55,835
-Let's do this.
-Let's go!

627
00:29:56,503 --> 00:29:58,463
We'll reach it in 30 minutes.

628
00:29:58,546 --> 00:29:59,380
<i>Ramyeon.</i>

629
00:30:00,256 --> 00:30:01,257
Dowoon, you go first.

630
00:30:01,341 --> 00:30:02,342
Okay.

631
00:30:02,425 --> 00:30:03,718
Take it slow.

632
00:30:04,385 --> 00:30:08,556
THE LEAD CHANGES

633
00:30:10,099 --> 00:30:11,518
-Go ahead.
-Okay.

634
00:30:15,063 --> 00:30:15,980
You can do it.

635
00:30:16,064 --> 00:30:17,065
Car-the, let's go.

636
00:30:18,733 --> 00:30:19,651
Let's go.

637
00:30:19,734 --> 00:30:20,568
Let's go.

638
00:30:21,778 --> 00:30:23,530
It sure is steep.

639
00:30:24,364 --> 00:30:25,573
My goodness.

640
00:30:26,950 --> 00:30:28,076
My gosh.

641
00:30:37,710 --> 00:30:39,045
-Chae-min, go first.
-Okay.

642
00:30:39,921 --> 00:30:40,797
It's hard, right?

643
00:30:41,464 --> 00:30:42,924
This is way too much.

644
00:30:44,217 --> 00:30:45,051
THE LEAD CHANGES

645
00:30:45,134 --> 00:30:46,469
Let me take out my poles too.

646
00:30:49,013 --> 00:30:51,391
Let's do this.

647
00:30:51,474 --> 00:30:54,936
THE STAFF MEMBERS ARE STARTING
TO FALL BEHIND TOO

648
00:30:57,730 --> 00:30:59,566
SIGHS

649
00:30:59,649 --> 00:31:00,483
<i>Ramyeon.</i>

650
00:31:01,109 --> 00:31:01,943
<i>Ramyeon.</i>

651
00:31:03,778 --> 00:31:08,241
TARZZAN'S CURRENT VIEW

652
00:31:08,324 --> 00:31:11,119
I'm not even exaggerating.
The path was full of rocks.

653
00:31:11,202 --> 00:31:12,287
I looked at the rocks

654
00:31:12,787 --> 00:31:16,040
and kept thinking,
"Which rock do I step on so I don't slip?"

655
00:31:16,541 --> 00:31:18,376
It made me

656
00:31:19,002 --> 00:31:23,548
focus a lot more than I thought.

657
00:31:23,631 --> 00:31:24,883
That's what I thought.

658
00:31:25,592 --> 00:31:26,467
So I decided

659
00:31:26,551 --> 00:31:30,263
to change my stage name.

660
00:31:31,222 --> 00:31:32,807
-Tarzzan.
-Yes?

661
00:31:33,808 --> 00:31:34,893
Yes?

662
00:31:34,976 --> 00:31:35,810
What?

663
00:31:36,311 --> 00:31:37,145
Oh…

664
00:31:39,939 --> 00:31:46,946
MEANWHILE, 1 PERSON CLIMBS UP STEADILY

665
00:31:51,659 --> 00:31:54,245
People are starting to fall behind
one by one.

666
00:31:55,121 --> 00:31:57,624
Who's the MVP among the members?

667
00:31:57,707 --> 00:31:58,541
Lee Chae-min.

668
00:31:59,334 --> 00:32:00,335
Wouldn't it be Chae-min?

669
00:32:00,418 --> 00:32:02,837
I don't remember him falling behind.

670
00:32:03,338 --> 00:32:06,424
Chae-min will really

671
00:32:07,967 --> 00:32:09,177
become successful.

672
00:32:10,553 --> 00:32:13,014
It looked like he was there
to shoot a commercial.

673
00:32:13,765 --> 00:32:17,560
LOOKING THIS GOOD AFTER 4 HOURS OF HIKING

674
00:32:18,561 --> 00:32:21,522
My calves hurt more than my thighs.

675
00:32:21,606 --> 00:32:24,359
Use all areas of your foot
to step on the ground.

676
00:32:24,442 --> 00:32:26,235
Don't just step on the ball of your foot.

677
00:32:26,319 --> 00:32:27,153
Really?

678
00:32:27,236 --> 00:32:29,155
If you do that, your calves will hurt.

679
00:32:30,490 --> 00:32:32,075
That's what it said on YouTube.

680
00:32:33,284 --> 00:32:35,244
I'm amazed that there's a path here.

681
00:32:36,663 --> 00:32:37,830
I wonder who paved it.

682
00:32:37,914 --> 00:32:38,748
Exactly.

683
00:32:40,375 --> 00:32:41,584
But isn't it really pretty?

684
00:32:41,668 --> 00:32:42,669
It is pretty.

685
00:32:43,336 --> 00:32:45,088
The sunlight

686
00:32:45,880 --> 00:32:46,965
reflected on the snow.

687
00:32:47,048 --> 00:32:48,257
How should I put it?

688
00:32:48,341 --> 00:32:49,467
I can't form a sentence.

689
00:32:49,968 --> 00:32:51,803
-Isn't it pretty back there?
-It really is.

690
00:32:54,430 --> 00:33:00,395
MEANWHILE, HE REALLY CAN'T FORM A SENTENCE

691
00:33:00,478 --> 00:33:04,107
GROANS

692
00:33:05,733 --> 00:33:06,818
I'm beyond my limits.

693
00:33:10,321 --> 00:33:11,322
Let's rest here.

694
00:33:12,657 --> 00:33:14,117
I don't think I can make it.

695
00:33:18,621 --> 00:33:19,831
It really is tough.

696
00:33:33,594 --> 00:33:37,098
HE SETS OFF AGAIN

697
00:33:38,307 --> 00:33:39,934
GROANS

698
00:33:40,018 --> 00:33:41,185
Hold on.

699
00:33:44,105 --> 00:33:45,690
My thighs are about to explode.

700
00:33:54,073 --> 00:33:56,034
Jung-won looks like he gave up.

701
00:33:58,286 --> 00:34:01,497
Will the other hikes be tougher than this?

702
00:34:04,125 --> 00:34:07,378
I lost some of my memories. Seriously.

703
00:34:07,920 --> 00:34:09,464
I think

704
00:34:09,964 --> 00:34:11,883
I asked the producer

705
00:34:12,842 --> 00:34:16,095
if any of the other hikes
would be tougher than this.

706
00:34:16,596 --> 00:34:18,139
Because even until then,

707
00:34:18,222 --> 00:34:20,349
I was determined to go to Producer Nah

708
00:34:20,433 --> 00:34:22,393
and tell him, "I really can't do this."

709
00:34:22,477 --> 00:34:26,147
I thought it'd be better to tell him
before the show became more concrete.

710
00:34:26,647 --> 00:34:28,816
I honestly thought that far.

711
00:34:28,900 --> 00:34:30,860
"I'll become a nuisance if I continue."

712
00:34:31,444 --> 00:34:32,862
Because I felt it myself.

713
00:34:33,946 --> 00:34:35,281
I kept whining.

714
00:34:35,364 --> 00:34:38,242
And I'm not even someone
who normally whines a lot.

715
00:34:46,042 --> 00:34:47,085
Goodness.

716
00:34:49,545 --> 00:34:50,630
This is too hard.

717
00:35:03,184 --> 00:35:05,186
Let's sit for a while. I'm beat as well.

718
00:35:11,275 --> 00:35:13,402
"If there were a chair here,

719
00:35:13,903 --> 00:35:15,238
I had warmer clothes on,

720
00:35:15,321 --> 00:35:17,156
and I wasn't filming,

721
00:35:17,240 --> 00:35:20,993
I could just sit here for a while,
stare at the view, and zone out."

722
00:35:21,077 --> 00:35:22,203
I had that thought.

723
00:35:23,496 --> 00:35:24,330
I mean,

724
00:35:25,206 --> 00:35:26,666
we're the protagonists.

725
00:35:27,583 --> 00:35:29,585
We can just hike according to our pace.

726
00:35:31,337 --> 00:35:32,713
I was holding onto the last straw.

727
00:35:32,797 --> 00:35:34,090
It's not like I can go down

728
00:35:34,173 --> 00:35:35,842
if I say I quit.

729
00:35:35,925 --> 00:35:38,970
Had there been an escalator,
I would've gone down immediately.

730
00:35:39,470 --> 00:35:41,305
"I'm really sorry. I mean it."

731
00:35:42,598 --> 00:35:44,809
But it's not like I could go down.

732
00:35:44,892 --> 00:35:45,726
And

733
00:35:46,227 --> 00:35:47,603
I was feeling a bit hungry.

734
00:35:48,646 --> 00:35:49,939
The other members had the food.

735
00:35:50,565 --> 00:35:51,858
I only had the plates.

736
00:35:52,900 --> 00:35:53,734
So…

737
00:35:55,653 --> 00:35:58,072
-Hold the poles shorter.
-Okay.

738
00:35:58,573 --> 00:36:00,491
Don't hold the poles like this.

739
00:36:00,575 --> 00:36:02,368
Imagine you're elderly and using a cane,

740
00:36:02,451 --> 00:36:03,661
and push like this.

741
00:36:04,162 --> 00:36:05,705
-Should I?
-It's a bit better.

742
00:36:05,788 --> 00:36:07,165
-Hold them shorter?
-Shorter.

743
00:36:07,248 --> 00:36:08,875
I'm holding them very short.

744
00:36:43,951 --> 00:36:47,538
THEY REGROUP WITH THE LEAD GROUP

745
00:36:48,331 --> 00:36:50,208
We're almost there, guys.

746
00:36:52,585 --> 00:36:54,462
We're moving faster
than the expected time.

747
00:36:54,545 --> 00:36:55,796
-Really?
-Really?

748
00:36:56,964 --> 00:36:58,883
Do you know what's important now?

749
00:36:58,966 --> 00:37:00,635
-What is it?
-I'm not even hungry.

750
00:37:01,344 --> 00:37:02,220
You know what I mean?

751
00:37:02,303 --> 00:37:03,429
I said the same thing.

752
00:37:03,512 --> 00:37:05,806
In this state,
I can't eat pork belly or whatnot.

753
00:37:07,475 --> 00:37:08,559
I'm not kidding.

754
00:37:09,477 --> 00:37:12,188
I might develop a mountain allergy.

755
00:37:13,564 --> 00:37:15,399
Forget about pork belly.

756
00:37:16,108 --> 00:37:17,526
I'm really

757
00:37:18,819 --> 00:37:20,529
resenting myself now.

758
00:37:22,281 --> 00:37:23,532
Shall we go?

759
00:37:24,367 --> 00:37:25,284
Let's go.

760
00:37:26,869 --> 00:37:28,955
But you'll end up enjoying it the most.

761
00:37:29,038 --> 00:37:30,289
I will eat some, I guess.

762
00:37:31,707 --> 00:37:33,251
It'll be delicious, of course.

763
00:37:34,752 --> 00:37:36,337
We just need to climb those stairs.

764
00:37:36,420 --> 00:37:38,464
How long is the staircase?

765
00:37:39,048 --> 00:37:40,007
That's a lie.

766
00:37:40,091 --> 00:37:41,759
About that being the last hurdle.

767
00:37:43,344 --> 00:37:44,303
Once we go up there,

768
00:37:44,387 --> 00:37:46,389
he'll say, "This is the last part."

769
00:37:47,556 --> 00:37:49,767
It looks like there'll be more stairs.

770
00:37:49,850 --> 00:37:52,687
What if it's a trick,
and there's something else

771
00:37:52,770 --> 00:37:53,854
after the staircase?

772
00:37:56,941 --> 00:38:03,364
FULL OF DOUBTS

773
00:38:07,785 --> 00:38:08,995
This isn't the shelter.

774
00:38:09,078 --> 00:38:10,621
This is the Huiungak Observatory Deck.

775
00:38:10,705 --> 00:38:11,539
I see.

776
00:38:14,500 --> 00:38:16,585
Have a look at the view.

777
00:38:17,169 --> 00:38:18,004
My gosh.

778
00:38:19,255 --> 00:38:20,131
Goodness.

779
00:38:20,631 --> 00:38:21,924
My gosh.

780
00:38:22,550 --> 00:38:23,384
This is amazing.

781
00:38:25,511 --> 00:38:26,554
It's nice.

782
00:38:43,487 --> 00:38:45,823
You might like this a little.

783
00:38:45,906 --> 00:38:48,534
I mean, I genuinely like it.

784
00:38:48,617 --> 00:38:50,953
But honestly speaking,

785
00:38:51,662 --> 00:38:52,955
it's not to that extent.

786
00:38:54,040 --> 00:38:55,750
Not worth the trouble.

787
00:38:57,585 --> 00:38:59,503
It reminds me of <i>Avatar.</i>

788
00:39:00,004 --> 00:39:00,838
Okay.

789
00:39:02,673 --> 00:39:08,054
AVATARZZAN ON SEORAKSAN

790
00:39:08,137 --> 00:39:10,806
It looked like a scene
from the movie <i>Avatar.</i>

791
00:39:10,890 --> 00:39:12,058
It was so pretty.

792
00:39:12,141 --> 00:39:17,313
I could see a stone mountain.

793
00:39:17,396 --> 00:39:20,608
<i>When I look up, I see snow.</i>
<i>When I look down, there's no snow.</i>

794
00:39:20,691 --> 00:39:22,360
<i>The view was really pretty.</i>

795
00:39:22,443 --> 00:39:25,821
<i>It made me think, "I'm really so high up."</i>

796
00:39:32,870 --> 00:39:37,458
THE OLDER MEMBERS WHO DON'T APPRECIATE
NICE VIEWS TAKE A PICTURE TOO

797
00:39:44,799 --> 00:39:47,968
STRIKING A CHEER-UP POSE FOR NO REASON

798
00:39:48,052 --> 00:39:52,932
JANUARY 12, 2026,
IN FRONT OF GONGNYONG RIDGE

799
00:39:53,015 --> 00:39:55,643
The pork belly must be frozen now.

800
00:39:57,520 --> 00:39:58,646
Everything froze.

801
00:40:00,272 --> 00:40:01,941
I went to the toilet,

802
00:40:02,441 --> 00:40:04,026
and it was steaming.

803
00:40:06,362 --> 00:40:07,363
Is it over there?

804
00:40:08,864 --> 00:40:11,075
We're here.

805
00:40:11,742 --> 00:40:13,077
It's pretty here.

806
00:40:27,967 --> 00:40:29,009
Good job.

807
00:40:30,136 --> 00:40:34,515
THEY FINALLY ARRIVE AT TODAY'S DESTINATION

808
00:40:34,598 --> 00:40:35,433
Good job.

809
00:40:35,516 --> 00:40:39,395
<i>This is the Huiungak Shelter</i>
<i>of Seoraksan National Park.</i>

810
00:40:39,478 --> 00:40:41,313
HUIUNGAK SHELTER

811
00:40:43,983 --> 00:40:44,817
CHEONBULDONGGYEGOK

812
00:40:44,900 --> 00:40:46,652
THE FINAL GATEWAY TO DAECHEONGBONG PEAK

813
00:40:47,653 --> 00:40:50,531
THE HUB OF SEORAKSAN TRAILS
LOCATED 1,065 M ABOVE SEA LEVEL

814
00:40:50,614 --> 00:40:52,283
<i>On your right is the kitchen.</i>

815
00:40:54,827 --> 00:40:57,997
A CLEAN COOKING AREA
PROVIDING WARM MEALS FOR HIKERS

816
00:40:58,080 --> 00:41:00,374
<i>And on your right is the accommodation.</i>

817
00:41:00,458 --> 00:41:02,209
CLEAN AND COZY ACCOMMODATION

818
00:41:02,293 --> 00:41:04,170
<i>There was an avalanche</i>
<i>on Seoraksan before.</i>

819
00:41:04,253 --> 00:41:07,256
A MEANINGFUL SHELTER BUILT
AFTER THE 1969 SEORAKSAN DISASTER

820
00:41:07,339 --> 00:41:09,133
<i>It's a meaningful shelter built after it.</i>

821
00:41:09,216 --> 00:41:11,260
<i>So it's the biggest</i>
<i>and has the best facilities.</i>

822
00:41:11,969 --> 00:41:15,890
THEY ARRIVED AT THE FINAL DESTINATION
OF THE TRAINING CAMP, HUIUNGAK SHELTER

823
00:41:15,973 --> 00:41:19,226
The goal was to arrive by 12:00 p.m.,
and we're 17 minutes early.

824
00:41:19,310 --> 00:41:20,561
THE CLUB MEMBERS ARE FAST

825
00:41:20,644 --> 00:41:22,188
We arrived much earlier than expected.

826
00:41:22,271 --> 00:41:24,231
How do those who work here commute?

827
00:41:24,315 --> 00:41:25,149
Do they hike?

828
00:41:25,232 --> 00:41:26,358
BY HIKING?

829
00:41:26,442 --> 00:41:28,903
From what I know,
they change shifts once a week.

830
00:41:28,986 --> 00:41:30,905
THAT'S AMAZING

831
00:41:31,697 --> 00:41:33,616
Where do we go in? To the right?

832
00:41:34,366 --> 00:41:35,868
Let's go somewhere warm.

833
00:41:36,368 --> 00:41:39,121
THE MEMBERS ARE EXHAUSTED
FROM THE LONG HIKE

834
00:41:41,165 --> 00:41:42,750
THEY ENTER THE KITCHEN WITH HIGH HOPES

835
00:41:42,833 --> 00:41:45,294
Finally. It already smells so good.

836
00:41:46,712 --> 00:41:47,671
Gosh.

837
00:41:47,755 --> 00:41:49,590
What's that? Is it here?

838
00:41:50,341 --> 00:41:52,092
THIS IS THE KITCHEN?

839
00:41:52,176 --> 00:41:53,010
It's a bit…

840
00:41:53,093 --> 00:41:54,428
This isn't what I expected.

841
00:41:54,512 --> 00:41:56,472
They won't have nice tables and chairs.

842
00:41:57,723 --> 00:41:59,141
<i>I thought we'd sit and eat</i>

843
00:41:59,808 --> 00:42:01,352
at the shelter.

844
00:42:01,852 --> 00:42:03,604
Since it was my first time there,

845
00:42:03,687 --> 00:42:05,397
I thought we'd sit and eat.

846
00:42:06,190 --> 00:42:07,858
I thought it was a waiting area,

847
00:42:08,359 --> 00:42:10,236
not a community kitchen.

848
00:42:10,319 --> 00:42:11,987
-Is that how it normally is?
-Yes.

849
00:42:13,739 --> 00:42:15,407
QUICKLY GETTING READY TO EAT

850
00:42:15,491 --> 00:42:16,575
Let's take them out.

851
00:42:17,201 --> 00:42:20,246
CAR, THE GARDEN IS IN CHARGE
OF THE CAMPING COOKSET AND GAS BURNER

852
00:42:20,329 --> 00:42:21,413
Water slushie.

853
00:42:21,914 --> 00:42:24,917
CHAE-MIN IS IN CHARGE OF RAMYEON AND MEAT

854
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:26,377
Did you cut it like this?

855
00:42:26,460 --> 00:42:28,379
I asked the butcher to cut it.

856
00:42:29,129 --> 00:42:31,549
TARZZAN, ALSO IN CHARGE OF MEAT,
CHECKS THE MEAT HE BOUGHT

857
00:42:32,132 --> 00:42:34,593
THEY PACKED A GENEROUS AMOUNT OF LUNCH

858
00:42:34,677 --> 00:42:35,844
Everything is prepared well.

859
00:42:38,097 --> 00:42:39,473
THE FIRE IGNITES AT DOWOON'S TOUCH

860
00:42:39,557 --> 00:42:40,891
-Like this?
-Thank you.

861
00:42:40,975 --> 00:42:42,393
-Shall I grill right away?
-Now?

862
00:42:42,476 --> 00:42:43,435
Shall we grill it now?

863
00:42:43,519 --> 00:42:46,105
PORK BELLY PARTY
GRILLED BY PRESIDENT TARZZAN

864
00:42:46,188 --> 00:42:47,022
The fire…

865
00:42:47,106 --> 00:42:48,440
HE CHECKS THE PAN'S TEMPERATURE

866
00:42:48,524 --> 00:42:50,067
I'm amazed there's signal here.

867
00:42:50,150 --> 00:42:51,110
It's hot.

868
00:42:52,861 --> 00:42:54,613
That sound.

869
00:42:54,697 --> 00:42:58,492
THE FIRST PORK BELLY ENTERS

870
00:43:00,452 --> 00:43:01,287
It's salty.

871
00:43:02,913 --> 00:43:04,623
SPRINKLING SALT

872
00:43:04,707 --> 00:43:08,252
Is there a plate
where I can place the grilled meat?

873
00:43:08,335 --> 00:43:09,295
-Yes.
-Is this okay?

874
00:43:09,378 --> 00:43:10,254
Yes, thank you.

875
00:43:11,797 --> 00:43:12,840
It smells amazing.

876
00:43:12,923 --> 00:43:15,593
A GENEROUS AMOUNT OF PEPPER

877
00:43:27,438 --> 00:43:29,273
Shall we try a piece each first?

878
00:43:29,356 --> 00:43:30,441
Try it first.

879
00:43:30,524 --> 00:43:32,526
TARZZAN'S GRILLED PORK BELLY IS COMPLETE

880
00:43:33,152 --> 00:43:36,530
THE FIRST PROPER MEAL
AFTER 5 HOURS OF HIKING

881
00:43:50,294 --> 00:43:51,587
It's tasty.

882
00:43:52,379 --> 00:43:53,213
This is crazy.

883
00:43:58,010 --> 00:43:58,844
It's good.

884
00:44:03,265 --> 00:44:06,518
PORK BELLY TASTES EVEN BETTER
AFTER WORKING OUT SO HARD

885
00:44:06,602 --> 00:44:08,646
-It's good.
-Goodness.

886
00:44:09,146 --> 00:44:11,523
My mind is starting to get clearer now.

887
00:44:20,366 --> 00:44:23,243
THEY CONTINUE TO CONSUME MEAT

888
00:44:25,204 --> 00:44:26,038
I grill meat well.

889
00:44:27,915 --> 00:44:28,749
I'll do it.

890
00:44:39,134 --> 00:44:41,345
HE'S BUSY EATING MEAT

891
00:44:41,428 --> 00:44:42,471
It sure is tasty.

892
00:44:42,554 --> 00:44:46,058
HE TAKES THE TONGS FROM TARZZAN

893
00:44:48,018 --> 00:44:49,853
Now the heat is stronger,
it grills better.

894
00:44:52,398 --> 00:44:53,399
This is it.

895
00:44:54,483 --> 00:44:59,405
CHAE-MIN'S GRILLED PORK BELLY
MAKES YOU SALIVATE

896
00:45:15,712 --> 00:45:18,048
It's perfectly seasoned.

897
00:45:19,341 --> 00:45:20,384
I'm satisfied.

898
00:45:22,094 --> 00:45:25,931
IT'S WORTH THE 5-HOUR HIKE

899
00:45:26,932 --> 00:45:27,975
It's delicious.

900
00:45:28,851 --> 00:45:30,894
Should we eat the field rations first?

901
00:45:30,978 --> 00:45:31,895
Do you want it?

902
00:45:31,979 --> 00:45:33,439
Since you brought it, let's eat it.

903
00:45:34,314 --> 00:45:35,357
DOWOON BROUGHT MRE

904
00:45:35,441 --> 00:45:36,733
Which one do you want?

905
00:45:37,359 --> 00:45:39,153
Two should be enough.

906
00:45:40,487 --> 00:45:41,947
"Open the heating element."

907
00:45:42,906 --> 00:45:44,366
What's this inside?

908
00:45:45,117 --> 00:45:46,493
-A heating element.
-Like that?

909
00:45:46,577 --> 00:45:48,912
COOKING MRE:
1. PLACE THE HEATING ELEMENT AT THE BOTTOM

910
00:45:48,996 --> 00:45:50,414
2. SET THE MRE AND POUR WATER

911
00:45:50,497 --> 00:45:52,332
Pouring water makes it heat up?

912
00:45:52,416 --> 00:45:53,292
That's strange.

913
00:45:53,375 --> 00:45:54,209
Is it working?

914
00:45:55,002 --> 00:45:55,836
Yes.

915
00:45:55,919 --> 00:45:57,212
3. WAIT FOR 10 MINUTES!

916
00:46:01,925 --> 00:46:03,302
How are you guys so fast?

917
00:46:03,385 --> 00:46:04,470
You're here.

918
00:46:04,970 --> 00:46:08,515
LOOKING HAGGARD

919
00:46:08,599 --> 00:46:11,018
Can you do more of this?

920
00:46:11,101 --> 00:46:12,394
No, I'm quitting the show.

921
00:46:13,353 --> 00:46:14,688
Have fun with the filming.

922
00:46:15,397 --> 00:46:16,732
Good luck with it.

923
00:46:17,649 --> 00:46:19,026
We'll join you and quit together.

924
00:46:20,068 --> 00:46:21,528
We can eat this now.

925
00:46:23,572 --> 00:46:24,865
It'll be like pouring hot water

926
00:46:25,532 --> 00:46:27,534
into a <i>ramyeon</i> bag.

927
00:46:28,243 --> 00:46:31,413
ROUND 2 STARTS

928
00:46:32,789 --> 00:46:33,749
How does it taste?

929
00:46:34,291 --> 00:46:35,417
Yes, it's like <i>ramyeon</i>

930
00:46:36,126 --> 00:46:37,419
if you pour water directly here.

931
00:46:44,593 --> 00:46:45,802
-Do you want <i>ramyeon?</i>
-Sorry?

932
00:46:45,886 --> 00:46:47,346
-Do you want <i>ramyeon?</i>
-Sure.

933
00:46:58,857 --> 00:47:00,025
Eat up.

934
00:47:00,108 --> 00:47:01,527
This is amazing.

935
00:47:01,610 --> 00:47:03,904
-It's good, right?
-This is it.

936
00:47:07,908 --> 00:47:09,868
How did we do, sir?

937
00:47:09,952 --> 00:47:13,288
You were much better than I thought.

938
00:47:15,165 --> 00:47:16,500
You hiked well.

939
00:47:16,583 --> 00:47:17,834
-The next mountain.
-Yes.

940
00:47:17,918 --> 00:47:19,670
Can it be lower?

941
00:47:22,673 --> 00:47:25,092
I couldn't hold myself back from cursing.

942
00:47:25,759 --> 00:47:26,593
I'm serious.

943
00:47:26,677 --> 00:47:28,470
You can curse if it's too hard.

944
00:47:29,346 --> 00:47:30,639
I can't hold it back.

945
00:47:30,722 --> 00:47:31,932
You can curse.

946
00:47:32,015 --> 00:47:34,101
I really don't get
why I need to climb up here.

947
00:47:35,018 --> 00:47:36,603
I thought I'd find the reason.

948
00:47:37,104 --> 00:47:38,605
I can't at all.

949
00:47:39,815 --> 00:47:41,024
It pisses me off so badly.

950
00:47:41,525 --> 00:47:42,484
The whole hike did.

951
00:47:43,819 --> 00:47:46,446
Are three packs of <i>ramyeon</i> enough?
Or four?

952
00:47:46,530 --> 00:47:47,364
Let's cook four.

953
00:47:47,447 --> 00:47:48,365
BECAUSE I'M PISSED

954
00:47:48,448 --> 00:47:49,783
Okay. You must be very hungry.

955
00:47:50,450 --> 00:47:54,496
ROUND 3, COOKING RAMYEON

956
00:47:54,580 --> 00:47:55,497
I'm putting it in.

957
00:47:55,581 --> 00:47:56,415
RAMYEON TIME

958
00:47:56,498 --> 00:47:58,208
Can I fit all four inside?

959
00:47:59,126 --> 00:47:59,960
Let's see how.

960
00:48:00,043 --> 00:48:01,587
SQUEEZE THEM IN FOR NOW

961
00:48:01,670 --> 00:48:02,754
There's no other way.

962
00:48:04,506 --> 00:48:05,716
-This…
-We can do it.

963
00:48:07,175 --> 00:48:08,218
Nice.

964
00:48:08,302 --> 00:48:10,971
Isn't there too little water
for the amount of noodles?

965
00:48:11,054 --> 00:48:12,472
Let's try it first.

966
00:48:12,556 --> 00:48:14,308
THE RAMYEON NOODLES HIDE THE SOUP

967
00:48:14,391 --> 00:48:16,101
-Just eat.
-It'll give you indigestion.

968
00:48:16,184 --> 00:48:17,060
It looks good.

969
00:48:18,228 --> 00:48:20,355
LET SOME AIR IN BY LIFTING IT UP AND DOWN

970
00:48:20,439 --> 00:48:22,065
I'll put the outer ones inside.

971
00:48:22,774 --> 00:48:23,650
I think it's cooked.

972
00:48:23,734 --> 00:48:24,568
I think it's ready.

973
00:48:24,651 --> 00:48:27,404
RAMYEON IS COMPLETE

974
00:48:27,487 --> 00:48:28,322
Thanks for the food.

975
00:48:28,405 --> 00:48:30,115
You better use this to scoop.

976
00:48:30,198 --> 00:48:31,325
Okay.

977
00:48:31,408 --> 00:48:35,203
HE LIFTS UP THE WELL-COOKED NOODLES

978
00:48:49,217 --> 00:48:51,803
IT DISAPPEARS LIKE MAGIC
AS SOON AS HE PUTS IT IN HIS MOUTH

979
00:48:52,929 --> 00:48:53,764
It's good.

980
00:48:57,476 --> 00:49:00,937
HE'S ABOUT TO GO INTO THE PLATE

981
00:49:01,021 --> 00:49:02,689
The pork belly was amazing,

982
00:49:03,273 --> 00:49:04,566
but the <i>ramyeon</i> was even better.

983
00:49:04,650 --> 00:49:05,984
-You ate nonstop.
-Yes.

984
00:49:06,610 --> 00:49:08,195
I told him to cook four.

985
00:49:16,662 --> 00:49:18,580
I eat a lot at home,

986
00:49:19,081 --> 00:49:21,083
but eating a lot after working out…

987
00:49:21,583 --> 00:49:22,459
You feel less guilty.

988
00:49:22,542 --> 00:49:23,877
I never feel guilty anyway.

989
00:49:25,504 --> 00:49:26,546
It just feels good.

990
00:49:28,924 --> 00:49:32,386
FEELING BETTER AFTER SOME RAMYEON

991
00:49:35,472 --> 00:49:37,307
Are we playing
Guess the Celebrities today?

992
00:49:37,391 --> 00:49:38,266
GUESS THE PERSON QUIZ

993
00:49:39,893 --> 00:49:42,979
NO
LET'S CLEAN UP AND DESCEND

994
00:49:43,063 --> 00:49:44,398
Where do I throw the food waste?

995
00:49:44,981 --> 00:49:47,234
They have a bin here.

996
00:49:47,317 --> 00:49:52,364
BEAUTIFUL PEOPLE CLEAN UP AFTER THEMSELVES

997
00:49:52,989 --> 00:49:53,949
Here are wet wipes.

998
00:49:55,325 --> 00:49:56,493
Anyone want wet wipes?

999
00:49:56,576 --> 00:49:57,411
Me.

1000
00:49:57,494 --> 00:49:58,537
Can I have one?

1001
00:50:00,580 --> 00:50:01,790
I have some too, but…

1002
00:50:02,499 --> 00:50:04,042
It's frozen, darn it.

1003
00:50:05,043 --> 00:50:05,919
Really?

1004
00:50:06,002 --> 00:50:06,837
A bit.

1005
00:50:06,920 --> 00:50:11,258
THE WET WIPES WON'T COME OUT

1006
00:50:11,341 --> 00:50:12,426
Really?

1007
00:50:13,260 --> 00:50:14,720
Did I pull it out the wrong way?

1008
00:50:14,803 --> 00:50:16,012
I don't think that's the case.

1009
00:50:16,972 --> 00:50:18,306
Right? It's…

1010
00:50:20,225 --> 00:50:21,351
Something's wrong.

1011
00:50:24,312 --> 00:50:25,147
They…

1012
00:50:25,689 --> 00:50:26,523
They became one.

1013
00:50:26,606 --> 00:50:27,566
Look at this.

1014
00:50:28,567 --> 00:50:29,735
They froze.

1015
00:50:30,235 --> 00:50:32,112
-What the heck?
-Gosh.

1016
00:50:32,195 --> 00:50:33,363
Look. They're frozen.

1017
00:50:33,905 --> 00:50:34,740
My gosh.

1018
00:50:36,366 --> 00:50:38,034
They won't budge.

1019
00:50:38,118 --> 00:50:39,536
I've never seen this happen.

1020
00:50:39,619 --> 00:50:41,329
The wet wipes are hard.

1021
00:50:41,413 --> 00:50:42,581
They won't come out.

1022
00:50:42,664 --> 00:50:44,875
MELTING WET WIPES WITH THEIR HANDS

1023
00:50:44,958 --> 00:50:46,418
It's like a dishcloth.

1024
00:50:46,501 --> 00:50:47,794
This is bad.

1025
00:50:48,670 --> 00:50:49,963
Wash your hands.

1026
00:50:51,131 --> 00:50:53,091
THEY WIPE THE TABLE USING ICE TISSUES

1027
00:50:53,967 --> 00:50:56,136
AND THROW THE TRASH INTO THE PLASTIC BAG

1028
00:50:56,219 --> 00:50:57,512
THEY'RE DONE TIDYING UP!

1029
00:50:57,596 --> 00:50:58,430
I'll carry it down.

1030
00:50:58,513 --> 00:50:59,890
It's fine.

1031
00:50:59,973 --> 00:51:01,057
Your bag is the heaviest.

1032
00:51:01,141 --> 00:51:02,684
THEY'RE FIGHTING TO TAKE THE BAG

1033
00:51:02,768 --> 00:51:03,935
I'll carry it.

1034
00:51:04,019 --> 00:51:05,187
No, it's fine.

1035
00:51:05,812 --> 00:51:07,397
HISSES

1036
00:51:07,481 --> 00:51:08,940
-Gosh.
-Don't do it.

1037
00:51:10,025 --> 00:51:13,737
TAKE THE TRASH,
AND THEY'RE REALLY DONE CLEANING!

1038
00:51:13,820 --> 00:51:19,826
1 HOUR 30 MINUTES IN THE SHELTER,
APPARENT TEMPERATURE -22℃

1039
00:51:21,036 --> 00:51:23,079
The tips of my hands and feet are…

1040
00:51:23,163 --> 00:51:24,289
They're now…

1041
00:51:24,372 --> 00:51:25,916
I can't feel them.

1042
00:51:26,625 --> 00:51:27,959
We have to go down quickly.

1043
00:51:29,377 --> 00:51:31,671
THE TEMPERATURE DROPPED
WHILE THEY WERE RESTING

1044
00:51:31,755 --> 00:51:33,965
THE SNOW AND WIND BECAME HARSHER

1045
00:51:34,674 --> 00:51:37,260
I think something's wrong
with the weather outside.

1046
00:51:38,553 --> 00:51:40,180
I was psychologically affected too.

1047
00:51:40,722 --> 00:51:43,266
Producer Nah said it first.

1048
00:51:43,350 --> 00:51:45,727
He said,
"This is too cold. This is impossible."

1049
00:51:45,811 --> 00:51:47,145
Firstly, my feet.

1050
00:51:47,646 --> 00:51:48,939
They were really cold.

1051
00:51:49,022 --> 00:51:50,106
My feet.

1052
00:51:52,359 --> 00:51:53,568
IT'S TIME TO DESCEND

1053
00:51:53,652 --> 00:51:54,903
I'm too scared to step outside.

1054
00:51:54,986 --> 00:51:56,112
Me too.

1055
00:51:58,782 --> 00:52:03,578
ASCENDING IS TOUGH,
AND DESCENDING IS DANGEROUS

1056
00:52:04,162 --> 00:52:05,789
Why didn't I bring my balaclava?

1057
00:52:05,872 --> 00:52:06,832
I'm a fool.

1058
00:52:07,833 --> 00:52:10,043
You still have your beard.

1059
00:52:10,126 --> 00:52:11,378
How would my beard…

1060
00:52:12,003 --> 00:52:13,880
My beard doesn't help at all.

1061
00:52:14,589 --> 00:52:16,216
Your beard doesn't help?

1062
00:52:16,967 --> 00:52:19,010
I think it does a little. No?

1063
00:52:20,011 --> 00:52:21,137
You…

1064
00:52:21,221 --> 00:52:22,472
Seriously!

1065
00:52:23,139 --> 00:52:23,974
What?

1066
00:52:24,057 --> 00:52:25,934
A BEARDED MAN MAKING FUN
OF ANOTHER BEARDED MAN

1067
00:52:26,017 --> 00:52:27,018
I don't even…

1068
00:52:29,729 --> 00:52:31,857
I don't even have the energy to talk back.

1069
00:52:35,735 --> 00:52:37,153
The real hell starts now.

1070
00:52:38,196 --> 00:52:41,074
<i>Honestly, that was</i>
<i>the most difficult crux.</i>

1071
00:52:41,157 --> 00:52:44,077
The cold I felt…

1072
00:52:44,661 --> 00:52:47,122
It felt like
my body temperature dropped rapidly,

1073
00:52:47,205 --> 00:52:49,249
as if I was getting hypothermia.

1074
00:52:50,000 --> 00:52:53,628
<i>So I wanted to move quickly.</i>

1075
00:52:53,712 --> 00:52:55,630
You feel less cold when you move.

1076
00:52:56,798 --> 00:53:00,176
WARMING UP THEIR BODIES BY MOVING

1077
00:53:00,260 --> 00:53:01,553
I can't feel my feet.

1078
00:53:02,053 --> 00:53:03,221
Me neither.

1079
00:53:03,305 --> 00:53:05,056
Doesn't your big toe hurt the most?

1080
00:53:05,140 --> 00:53:07,350
I can't feel my feet at all.

1081
00:53:07,851 --> 00:53:10,562
It was really excruciating
when we left the shelter.

1082
00:53:11,146 --> 00:53:14,608
For me, descending was harder
than ascending.

1083
00:53:16,234 --> 00:53:17,944
"It's insanely cold."

1084
00:53:18,028 --> 00:53:19,404
I had that thought.

1085
00:53:20,196 --> 00:53:21,698
<i>I was surprised too.</i>

1086
00:53:21,781 --> 00:53:23,950
It usually starts to get cold
in the afternoon.

1087
00:53:24,034 --> 00:53:27,370
When I go fishing, I feel chilly
in late afternoons.

1088
00:53:27,454 --> 00:53:29,331
-The sweat cools down and you feel cold.
-Yes.

1089
00:53:29,414 --> 00:53:32,083
Then fishing and hiking are a bit similar.

1090
00:53:32,167 --> 00:53:33,168
THEY'RE SIMILAR

1091
00:53:33,251 --> 00:53:34,586
In terms of temperature.

1092
00:53:35,086 --> 00:53:38,298
But fishing gives you
such a dopamine rush.

1093
00:53:38,381 --> 00:53:39,799
It's different from hiking.

1094
00:53:39,883 --> 00:53:40,717
RETRACTING HIS WORDS

1095
00:53:40,800 --> 00:53:42,385
Fishing is a 12-hour dopamine provider.

1096
00:53:42,469 --> 00:53:44,346
I catch yellowtail, you know.

1097
00:53:44,429 --> 00:53:45,722
I'm constantly doing this.

1098
00:53:45,805 --> 00:53:47,599
That makes you heat up.

1099
00:53:47,682 --> 00:53:49,643
That's similar to hiking. You keep moving.

1100
00:53:49,726 --> 00:53:50,936
CHANGING HIS WORDS AGAIN

1101
00:53:51,019 --> 00:53:53,897
But you have a cabin on a boat.

1102
00:53:53,980 --> 00:53:55,190
So it's quite comfortable.

1103
00:53:55,273 --> 00:53:57,233
Fishing is… Yes…

1104
00:53:58,068 --> 00:53:59,527
It's easier than hiking.

1105
00:53:59,611 --> 00:54:00,654
It's kind.

1106
00:54:00,737 --> 00:54:02,364
GOING BACK ON HIS WORDS ONCE AGAIN

1107
00:54:03,657 --> 00:54:05,200
Let's go.

1108
00:54:07,369 --> 00:54:11,456
THEY START TO DESCEND

1109
00:54:18,129 --> 00:54:21,508
HUIUNGAK SHELTER

1110
00:54:21,591 --> 00:54:25,261
GOING BACK TO THE STARTING POINT
TAKES ABOUT 4 HOURS 30 MINUTES

1111
00:54:25,345 --> 00:54:29,516
WHY IS DESCENDING DANGEROUS?

1112
00:54:32,018 --> 00:54:34,437
1. MUSCLES STIFFEN UP WHILE YOU REST

1113
00:54:34,521 --> 00:54:35,647
I'm already tired.

1114
00:54:36,898 --> 00:54:37,857
I feel cold.

1115
00:54:37,941 --> 00:54:40,151
2. YOUR BODY HAS COOLED DOWN

1116
00:54:40,986 --> 00:54:42,904
SLIPPERY

1117
00:54:42,988 --> 00:54:43,822
It's slippery.

1118
00:54:43,905 --> 00:54:45,156
3. THE GROUND HAS FROZEN

1119
00:54:45,824 --> 00:54:47,492
Going down is going to be hard.

1120
00:54:47,575 --> 00:54:48,410
I know, right?

1121
00:54:49,995 --> 00:54:51,788
I'll probably fall sick tomorrow.

1122
00:54:51,871 --> 00:54:53,081
-Same.
-Same.

1123
00:54:53,164 --> 00:54:56,668
I've already started coughing
and getting a runny nose.

1124
00:54:58,503 --> 00:54:59,337
SNIFFING

1125
00:54:59,421 --> 00:55:03,591
WHAT WAS DOWNHILL WHILE ASCENDING
NOW BECOMES UPHILL

1126
00:55:04,843 --> 00:55:06,720
It's so hard going uphill now.

1127
00:55:06,803 --> 00:55:07,971
Gosh.

1128
00:55:08,054 --> 00:55:10,015
LAUGHING IN DISMAY

1129
00:55:10,098 --> 00:55:14,185
THE SNOW PILED UP EVEN MORE
WHILE THEY WERE RESTING

1130
00:55:15,145 --> 00:55:18,314
GROANS

1131
00:55:18,398 --> 00:55:20,066
My thighs feel tight already.

1132
00:55:20,608 --> 00:55:23,737
YOU WERE HAVING A HARD TIME
AS SOON AS YOU STARTED TO DESCEND

1133
00:55:23,820 --> 00:55:24,696
Well, it's…

1134
00:55:24,779 --> 00:55:25,864
LAUGHING

1135
00:55:25,947 --> 00:55:27,073
Like this…

1136
00:55:27,157 --> 00:55:27,991
How should I say it?

1137
00:55:28,074 --> 00:55:30,160
When you pour water to clean dirt,

1138
00:55:31,036 --> 00:55:33,079
it floats away like this.

1139
00:55:34,456 --> 00:55:36,374
Yes, it felt like I was swept away.

1140
00:55:40,628 --> 00:55:44,340
GETTING SWEPT AWAY

1141
00:55:44,424 --> 00:55:48,261
WALKING CAREFULLY WITH FRAGILE LEGS

1142
00:55:49,387 --> 00:55:50,472
This is hard.

1143
00:55:52,140 --> 00:55:54,726
THE YOUNGEST MEMBERS FIND IT HARD TOO

1144
00:55:55,393 --> 00:55:57,062
SHOCKINGLY, A HIKER IN JEANS EXISTS

1145
00:55:57,145 --> 00:55:58,271
Car-the.

1146
00:55:58,354 --> 00:55:59,189
Yes?

1147
00:56:00,231 --> 00:56:01,524
It's different, right?

1148
00:56:01,608 --> 00:56:03,526
-It's different.
-It's different from going up.

1149
00:56:07,322 --> 00:56:08,281
Hello.

1150
00:56:09,282 --> 00:56:12,744
STILL POLITE

1151
00:56:15,705 --> 00:56:19,918
HE'S SWEPT AWAY, MAKING HIS
THOROUGH PREPARATIONS REDUNDANT

1152
00:56:20,460 --> 00:56:23,755
THEY'VE ONLY MOVED 200 M

1153
00:56:25,715 --> 00:56:29,677
THEY START GOING DOWN THE STEEP PASS

1154
00:56:29,761 --> 00:56:32,013
Why does it feel like
more snow has piled up?

1155
00:56:32,097 --> 00:56:34,265
My knees do feel the pain.

1156
00:56:34,349 --> 00:56:35,183
Me too.

1157
00:56:38,853 --> 00:56:40,522
Still, going down is much easier.

1158
00:56:40,605 --> 00:56:41,439
Exactly.

1159
00:56:43,983 --> 00:56:45,819
We climbed up so high.

1160
00:56:46,444 --> 00:56:49,239
HUIUNGAK SHELTER

1161
00:56:49,322 --> 00:56:51,407
CURRENT LOCATION

1162
00:56:51,908 --> 00:56:52,742
WHERE THEY'LL GO

1163
00:56:52,826 --> 00:56:54,410
<i>There's no end to the descent.</i>

1164
00:56:55,620 --> 00:56:57,205
We really climbed up here?

1165
00:56:58,248 --> 00:56:59,415
AMAZED AT HIS PAST SELF

1166
00:56:59,499 --> 00:57:01,960
Isn't it impressive
that we climbed up here?

1167
00:57:02,043 --> 00:57:03,837
Exactly. How did we do it?

1168
00:57:03,920 --> 00:57:05,296
I'm surprised too.

1169
00:57:05,380 --> 00:57:06,548
THEY CROSS THE STEEP AREA

1170
00:57:06,631 --> 00:57:08,466
I think we're done with the steep areas.

1171
00:57:08,550 --> 00:57:10,093
That was the steepest path.

1172
00:57:10,176 --> 00:57:11,177
Really?

1173
00:57:12,053 --> 00:57:14,222
Remember where you took photos and rested?

1174
00:57:14,305 --> 00:57:15,140
Yes.

1175
00:57:15,223 --> 00:57:18,434
THEY FACE THE VERY STEEP PATH AGAIN

1176
00:57:18,518 --> 00:57:20,603
Doesn't that mean
we came down really quickly?

1177
00:57:20,687 --> 00:57:21,855
You're going really fast.

1178
00:57:22,647 --> 00:57:24,190
-We walked nonstop.
-Yes.

1179
00:57:24,274 --> 00:57:26,359
1 HOUR TO GO UP, 25 MINUTES TO COME DOWN

1180
00:57:27,527 --> 00:57:28,486
Seriously…

1181
00:57:29,237 --> 00:57:30,238
Why do people climb up?

1182
00:57:30,822 --> 00:57:32,824
HE SUDDENLY ASKS A FUNDAMENTAL QUESTION

1183
00:57:32,907 --> 00:57:34,367
I really don't understand.

1184
00:57:36,119 --> 00:57:38,872
I probably won't find the answer
until the show ends.

1185
00:57:39,706 --> 00:57:41,249
I want to ride a sleigh.

1186
00:57:41,332 --> 00:57:44,836
I wish Siberian Huskies
would pull me down on a sled.

1187
00:57:44,919 --> 00:57:46,588
I start thinking about tricks.

1188
00:57:46,671 --> 00:57:49,507
"I'll bring skis next time

1189
00:57:49,591 --> 00:57:51,759
and ride them down."

1190
00:57:52,844 --> 00:57:56,014
More than being exhausted,
I felt so annoyed.

1191
00:57:56,097 --> 00:57:59,434
I hate boring stuff,
and I have to keep doing something new.

1192
00:57:59,517 --> 00:58:01,811
When you go up,
you're still doing something new,

1193
00:58:01,895 --> 00:58:03,938
so I found everything fascinating.

1194
00:58:04,022 --> 00:58:06,733
But when I was going down,
everything was annoying.

1195
00:58:06,816 --> 00:58:09,777
And the path felt three times longer.

1196
00:58:14,032 --> 00:58:14,949
It's nice.

1197
00:58:15,033 --> 00:58:16,659
It's so nice to see flat ground.

1198
00:58:19,245 --> 00:58:21,122
A fleeting moment of happiness.

1199
00:58:23,875 --> 00:58:25,210
It's a happy path.

1200
00:58:25,293 --> 00:58:26,127
Happy path.

1201
00:58:27,837 --> 00:58:30,673
A flat path is definitely better
than downhill.

1202
00:58:31,799 --> 00:58:33,635
Good, let's keep this up.

1203
00:58:34,636 --> 00:58:36,429
That will never happen.

1204
00:58:36,513 --> 00:58:37,722
Please, I beg you.

1205
00:58:37,805 --> 00:58:39,891
Just keep it this way. Don't make a fuss.

1206
00:58:41,059 --> 00:58:42,519
Mountain, please.

1207
00:58:43,561 --> 00:58:45,980
Is there a non-stone mountain?

1208
00:58:46,481 --> 00:58:47,482
A lot.

1209
00:58:47,982 --> 00:58:52,320
If there's "ak" in the mountain name,
that means it's a stone mountain.

1210
00:58:52,403 --> 00:58:53,446
Like Chiaksan?

1211
00:58:53,530 --> 00:58:54,531
Yes.

1212
00:58:54,614 --> 00:58:56,533
The "ak" mountains are the tough ones.

1213
00:58:57,742 --> 00:59:03,248
ENTERING THE SECTION
WHICH MAKES THEM SCREAM "AK"

1214
00:59:03,331 --> 00:59:05,833
A DANGEROUS COMBINATION OF ROCKS AND ICE

1215
00:59:05,917 --> 00:59:07,961
CHAE-MIN WALKS BACKWARD

1216
00:59:08,044 --> 00:59:10,296
TARZZAN JUMPS OVER IT

1217
00:59:10,380 --> 00:59:13,466
ADJUSTING HIS SAGGING PANTS

1218
00:59:14,717 --> 00:59:16,177
It's this stairway.

1219
00:59:16,970 --> 00:59:18,763
My thighs hurt now.

1220
00:59:22,809 --> 00:59:23,726
This…

1221
00:59:25,395 --> 00:59:27,105
Remember Cheondangpokpo Falls?

1222
00:59:27,605 --> 00:59:30,024
Why do you keep bringing up
Cheondangpokpo Falls?

1223
00:59:30,108 --> 00:59:31,568
LAUGHING

1224
00:59:31,651 --> 00:59:34,195
We'll drink water and rest
in Yangpok Shelter for a bit.

1225
00:59:34,279 --> 00:59:35,947
FOLLOW THE STAIRWAY TO YANGPOK SHELTER

1226
00:59:37,991 --> 00:59:39,450
TURNING AROUND

1227
00:59:40,827 --> 00:59:41,869
-Are you okay?
-Sorry?

1228
00:59:41,953 --> 00:59:43,329
-Are you okay?
-Yes.

1229
00:59:43,413 --> 00:59:44,789
A SWEET GUY

1230
00:59:45,373 --> 00:59:47,083
I don't think you're okay, though.

1231
00:59:48,585 --> 00:59:49,794
I'm not okay.

1232
00:59:54,591 --> 00:59:55,425
YANGPOK SHELTER

1233
00:59:55,508 --> 00:59:57,427
THEY ARRIVE AT YANGPOK SHELTER

1234
00:59:59,679 --> 01:00:01,764
We came down from such a high place?

1235
01:00:01,848 --> 01:00:02,724
That's amazing.

1236
01:00:02,807 --> 01:00:04,601
Where exactly were we?

1237
01:00:05,602 --> 01:00:08,021
Over and around that peak.

1238
01:00:08,938 --> 01:00:10,857
1 HOUR 10 MINUTES INTO DESCENT

1239
01:00:10,940 --> 01:00:11,774
I don't know either.

1240
01:00:12,442 --> 01:00:14,277
This is bad. When this goes on air…

1241
01:00:14,360 --> 01:00:17,280
I whined so much. I'm in trouble.

1242
01:00:17,822 --> 01:00:19,115
HE REGRETS WHINING

1243
01:00:19,198 --> 01:00:20,742
My thighs feel better after resting.

1244
01:00:21,326 --> 01:00:23,328
Car-the, get a grip.

1245
01:00:24,287 --> 01:00:25,872
Your eyes look hollow now.

1246
01:00:29,876 --> 01:00:30,752
I feel a bit sad.

1247
01:00:32,879 --> 01:00:33,880
Are you okay?

1248
01:00:33,963 --> 01:00:35,548
Yes, I feel great.

1249
01:00:35,632 --> 01:00:36,549
Dowoon is freaky…

1250
01:00:36,633 --> 01:00:37,800
I mean, he is fine.

1251
01:00:39,010 --> 01:00:39,927
CAR, THE BADMOUTHER

1252
01:00:40,011 --> 01:00:41,137
He's fine.

1253
01:00:43,306 --> 01:00:44,515
Dowoon is perfectly fine.

1254
01:00:44,599 --> 01:00:45,433
CONTINUE WALKING

1255
01:00:51,814 --> 01:00:53,441
FALLING DOWN

1256
01:00:54,484 --> 01:00:55,318
Be careful.

1257
01:00:56,194 --> 01:00:57,278
It's cold.

1258
01:00:57,362 --> 01:00:58,863
-Are you okay?
-Yes, I'm fine.

1259
01:00:59,864 --> 01:01:01,824
Watch out. You're worth a lot.

1260
01:01:01,908 --> 01:01:02,742
He's right.

1261
01:01:03,451 --> 01:01:04,827
So how much?

1262
01:01:04,911 --> 01:01:06,037
I don't know.

1263
01:01:14,671 --> 01:01:18,174
ADJUSTING HIS SAGGING PANTS AGAIN

1264
01:01:18,925 --> 01:01:20,218
It looks uncomfortable.

1265
01:01:21,094 --> 01:01:22,720
Isn't this where my hat flew away?

1266
01:01:22,804 --> 01:01:23,888
That's right.

1267
01:01:23,971 --> 01:01:25,390
We really pushed ourselves to hike.

1268
01:01:25,473 --> 01:01:27,809
THE ORYEONPOKPO FALLS STAIRCASE
WHERE TARZZAN LOST HIS HAT

1269
01:01:44,951 --> 01:01:47,495
ARRIVED AT GWIMYEONAM ROCK
2 HOURS INTO DESCENT

1270
01:01:47,578 --> 01:01:51,374
THEY STILL HAVE ABOUT 4.5 KM LEFT

1271
01:01:52,250 --> 01:01:54,043
I thought we were almost there.

1272
01:01:54,711 --> 01:01:55,586
Let's go quickly.

1273
01:01:57,964 --> 01:02:00,633
AFTER A QUICK BREAK, THEY SET OFF AGAIN.

1274
01:02:01,926 --> 01:02:03,344
-My hat--
-What strong wind.

1275
01:02:05,972 --> 01:02:07,682
I think we're near the ground.

1276
01:02:08,683 --> 01:02:10,601
The hiking trail should appear soon.

1277
01:02:11,102 --> 01:02:12,437
-The walking trail?
-Yes.

1278
01:02:14,397 --> 01:02:15,273
We're here.

1279
01:02:15,356 --> 01:02:16,190
We're not.

1280
01:02:17,316 --> 01:02:18,735
We must be almost there.

1281
01:02:19,986 --> 01:02:21,028
There's no snow now.

1282
01:02:21,112 --> 01:02:22,697
GETTING TRICKED BY EVERY FLAT GROUND

1283
01:02:26,242 --> 01:02:28,536
REMOVING CRAMPONS

1284
01:02:29,454 --> 01:02:31,122
-Let's do this!
-Let's go!

1285
01:02:31,205 --> 01:02:33,541
CHEERING THEMSELVES UP FOR THE LAST SPURT

1286
01:02:33,624 --> 01:02:36,669
If we still had an hour left to go,
I couldn't have cheered myself up.

1287
01:02:36,753 --> 01:02:38,212
One hour…

1288
01:02:38,296 --> 01:02:39,505
THEY DO HAVE 1 HOUR MORE TO GO

1289
01:02:39,589 --> 01:02:41,340
It feels weird without crampons.

1290
01:02:42,800 --> 01:02:43,968
It feels endless.

1291
01:02:44,844 --> 01:02:46,387
I miss walking on flat ground.

1292
01:02:56,105 --> 01:02:58,691
Is this mountain really for beginners?

1293
01:02:59,317 --> 01:03:01,068
-It's not.
-Goodness.

1294
01:03:01,152 --> 01:03:02,779
-Definitely not.
-I don't think so.

1295
01:03:02,862 --> 01:03:04,572
ChatGPT said not at all.

1296
01:03:05,072 --> 01:03:07,033
Right? This doesn't make sense.

1297
01:03:07,116 --> 01:03:09,285
It said us going to Huiungak Shelter

1298
01:03:09,994 --> 01:03:13,998
wasn't impossible,
but it was strongly against it.

1299
01:03:14,665 --> 01:03:16,667
And what are they going to air on TV?

1300
01:03:16,751 --> 01:03:18,628
Exactly. I'm curious about that too.

1301
01:03:18,711 --> 01:03:19,837
What we're doing now.

1302
01:03:19,921 --> 01:03:21,422
WHAT WE'RE DOING RIGHT NOW

1303
01:03:21,506 --> 01:03:23,466
The feeling of stepping on rocks…

1304
01:03:24,050 --> 01:03:25,218
I want flat ground.

1305
01:03:25,301 --> 01:03:26,803
I hate the rocks.

1306
01:03:27,887 --> 01:03:29,263
I really want

1307
01:03:29,764 --> 01:03:31,265
to kick these rocks really hard.

1308
01:03:31,349 --> 01:03:32,892
But it'll only hurt my foot.

1309
01:03:33,392 --> 01:03:34,393
I guess.

1310
01:03:34,477 --> 01:03:35,603
I really want

1311
01:03:36,103 --> 01:03:37,313
to hit the rocks.

1312
01:03:38,272 --> 01:03:39,690
Like this. I'm serious.

1313
01:03:40,566 --> 01:03:41,400
I mean it.

1314
01:03:42,068 --> 01:03:42,902
Goodness.

1315
01:03:43,986 --> 01:03:46,697
Dowoon, I see the Buddha statue area.

1316
01:03:48,115 --> 01:03:49,367
Look. It's flat ground.

1317
01:03:49,450 --> 01:03:50,535
THE TRAIL IS NEARBY

1318
01:03:50,618 --> 01:03:51,452
-Finally.
-I'm glad.

1319
01:03:51,536 --> 01:03:52,954
-I could run to it.
-Finally.

1320
01:03:53,037 --> 01:03:54,205
We escaped.

1321
01:03:54,956 --> 01:03:55,790
We're here.

1322
01:03:55,873 --> 01:04:00,837
AFTER ABOUT 3 HOURS OF DESCENDING,
THEY ARRIVE AT THE FLAT PATH

1323
01:04:01,712 --> 01:04:02,672
It's a flat path.

1324
01:04:06,092 --> 01:04:07,802
How long has it been
since I stepped on it?

1325
01:04:08,302 --> 01:04:09,136
I know, right?

1326
01:04:12,974 --> 01:04:14,725
TRIPPING

1327
01:04:14,809 --> 01:04:16,978
The rock tripped me again.

1328
01:04:20,189 --> 01:04:22,817
I really respect the cameraman.

1329
01:04:22,900 --> 01:04:24,819
-The cameraman…
-You're so impressive.

1330
01:04:25,903 --> 01:04:27,405
The audio director too.

1331
01:04:27,488 --> 01:04:29,365
The audio director is amazing too.

1332
01:04:29,448 --> 01:04:30,575
I really wish

1333
01:04:31,450 --> 01:04:32,451
it's something like this.

1334
01:04:32,535 --> 01:04:33,744
"You worked hard."

1335
01:04:33,828 --> 01:04:36,038
"Actually, we're not a hiking show."

1336
01:04:36,539 --> 01:04:38,875
"We go to places
with 'san' in their name."

1337
01:04:38,958 --> 01:04:42,086
Next, we'll go to Busan.
How nice would that be, right?

1338
01:04:42,169 --> 01:04:43,838
Ulsan, Busan, Masan.

1339
01:04:43,921 --> 01:04:45,756
We'll go to Ulsan next.

1340
01:04:45,840 --> 01:04:47,508
A VERY WRONG ASSUMPTION

1341
01:04:47,592 --> 01:04:49,176
They chose here first to piss us off.

1342
01:04:53,139 --> 01:04:55,641
TURNING AROUND

1343
01:04:55,725 --> 01:04:57,727
Go ahead. I'm fine.

1344
01:04:58,394 --> 01:04:59,228
Get going.

1345
01:04:59,312 --> 01:05:00,771
<i>Everyone walked so fast.</i>

1346
01:05:00,855 --> 01:05:01,981
I'm fine.

1347
01:05:02,064 --> 01:05:03,983
I prefer everyone to do what they want.

1348
01:05:04,066 --> 01:05:05,568
Whoever wants to go fast, go ahead.

1349
01:05:05,651 --> 01:05:07,236
I'll take my time.

1350
01:05:07,320 --> 01:05:09,614
But the path didn't end.

1351
01:05:10,656 --> 01:05:12,033
Was this track this long?

1352
01:05:13,200 --> 01:05:14,035
My thoughts exactly.

1353
01:05:14,827 --> 01:05:16,412
Why are my legs giving up on me?

1354
01:05:16,913 --> 01:05:17,997
I'm really at my limit.

1355
01:05:19,832 --> 01:05:22,168
Why does this path seem endless?

1356
01:05:22,877 --> 01:05:23,878
Did someone extend it?

1357
01:05:23,961 --> 01:05:25,963
It's about time Buddha appears.

1358
01:05:26,047 --> 01:05:27,256
Exactly.

1359
01:05:27,340 --> 01:05:28,925
He should appear soon.

1360
01:05:29,008 --> 01:05:30,885
This place is insane.

1361
01:05:30,968 --> 01:05:32,929
He should be here by now.

1362
01:05:33,012 --> 01:05:36,390
It was about time Buddha showed up,
but he wouldn't.

1363
01:05:37,767 --> 01:05:40,895
I'm Catholic,
but I desperately looked for Buddha.

1364
01:05:41,479 --> 01:05:43,022
I'm Christian,

1365
01:05:43,105 --> 01:05:45,232
but I really wanted to see Buddha.

1366
01:05:45,900 --> 01:05:47,318
When will the statue show up?

1367
01:05:47,818 --> 01:05:48,653
Seriously.

1368
01:05:48,736 --> 01:05:50,112
Stop it now.

1369
01:05:51,155 --> 01:05:52,865
Seriously, where did the statue go?

1370
01:05:52,949 --> 01:05:54,367
Did someone move it away?

1371
01:05:56,243 --> 01:05:57,161
I mean…

1372
01:05:57,244 --> 01:05:59,580
Someone must've moved it. I'm sure.

1373
01:05:59,664 --> 01:06:02,583
NOBODY MOVED IT

1374
01:06:04,043 --> 01:06:06,128
I want to end this show happily.

1375
01:06:09,590 --> 01:06:11,175
I want to keep my relationship

1376
01:06:11,968 --> 01:06:15,471
with Egg is Coming
as something positive and precious.

1377
01:06:16,013 --> 01:06:18,557
Let's go to Tarzzan's house

1378
01:06:19,600 --> 01:06:21,894
in Ulsan and eat.

1379
01:06:21,978 --> 01:06:24,480
Yes, and play Guess the Celebrities
with my parents.

1380
01:06:24,563 --> 01:06:25,982
Yes, play it with your parents.

1381
01:06:26,065 --> 01:06:27,692
I want to film <i>Earth Arcade.</i>

1382
01:06:28,693 --> 01:06:29,568
Seriously.

1383
01:06:30,528 --> 01:06:31,862
I'm serious.

1384
01:06:31,946 --> 01:06:33,572
I'm so envious of them.

1385
01:06:34,073 --> 01:06:36,033
I remember them smiling all the time.

1386
01:06:36,117 --> 01:06:37,034
I know, right?

1387
01:06:37,118 --> 01:06:38,077
-Right?
-Yes.

1388
01:06:38,160 --> 01:06:40,454
Lee Young-ji was always smiling.

1389
01:06:41,247 --> 01:06:43,624
Producer Nah looked happy then too.

1390
01:06:43,708 --> 01:06:44,709
Yes.

1391
01:06:44,792 --> 01:06:47,420
But he looked sick and tired today.

1392
01:06:48,421 --> 01:06:49,714
I see it.

1393
01:06:49,797 --> 01:06:52,008
THEY FINALLY ENCOUNTER THE BUDDHA STATUE

1394
01:06:52,091 --> 01:06:54,051
Earlier, why didn't Buddha…

1395
01:06:54,135 --> 01:06:56,262
-Stop us from going up.
-Why didn't he stop us?

1396
01:06:58,347 --> 01:06:59,640
We're almost there.

1397
01:06:59,724 --> 01:07:02,184
See, it's long again.

1398
01:07:02,268 --> 01:07:03,227
What…

1399
01:07:03,310 --> 01:07:05,062
-Wasn't this the end?
-Exactly.

1400
01:07:05,146 --> 01:07:06,105
The entrance is gone.

1401
01:07:06,188 --> 01:07:07,606
HYPNOTIZED 500 M FROM THE ENTRANCE

1402
01:07:09,567 --> 01:07:10,401
We're here.

1403
01:07:17,366 --> 01:07:18,617
Good job, everyone.

1404
01:07:18,701 --> 01:07:20,494
-Good job.
-We did great.

1405
01:07:20,578 --> 01:07:21,662
CURRENT TIME: 4:32 P.M.

1406
01:07:21,746 --> 01:07:23,497
9 HOURS 32 MINUTES TAKEN,
TRAINING CAMP ENDS

1407
01:07:23,581 --> 01:07:27,001
Q. WHAT ARE YOUR THOUGHTS
ON YOUR FIRST HIKE?

1408
01:07:27,585 --> 01:07:28,753
I did it.

1409
01:07:28,836 --> 01:07:32,381
I had this fear inside me.

1410
01:07:32,465 --> 01:07:34,300
I couldn't overcome it completely…

1411
01:07:34,383 --> 01:07:35,634
Is "overcome" correct? "Fight"?

1412
01:07:36,135 --> 01:07:38,429
Anyway, I couldn't do that,

1413
01:07:38,512 --> 01:07:40,389
but I managed to take a step forward,

1414
01:07:40,473 --> 01:07:42,767
which is really important for me.

1415
01:07:42,850 --> 01:07:45,186
I was very grateful for it.

1416
01:07:46,312 --> 01:07:47,646
Although it was tough,

1417
01:07:48,773 --> 01:07:50,107
it did heal me.

1418
01:07:50,191 --> 01:07:52,193
I felt like I became healthy.

1419
01:07:53,319 --> 01:07:56,072
Make sure to bring poles and a balaclava.

1420
01:07:56,155 --> 01:07:57,656
The brand doesn't matter.

1421
01:07:57,740 --> 01:07:59,116
Whether it's K2 or Salomon.

1422
01:07:59,742 --> 01:08:02,286
I may have been the president,

1423
01:08:03,079 --> 01:08:06,791
but Car-the showed great leadership.

1424
01:08:06,874 --> 01:08:11,378
I honestly didn't think
he'd make it until the end.

1425
01:08:12,046 --> 01:08:14,298
It was really tough.

1426
01:08:14,381 --> 01:08:18,594
But I think I overcame it smoothly.

1427
01:08:18,677 --> 01:08:21,472
Why do you think people hike?

1428
01:08:22,681 --> 01:08:23,933
I wonder why.

1429
01:08:26,644 --> 01:08:28,020
The title is really fitting.

1430
01:08:28,104 --> 01:08:30,231
<i>Take a Hike!</i> Why do people hike?

1431
01:08:31,482 --> 01:08:32,316
I don't know.

1432
01:08:32,817 --> 01:08:33,651
I have no clue.

1433
01:08:34,693 --> 01:08:38,405
Hiking empties your mind.

1434
01:08:38,989 --> 01:08:40,116
Because it's tough.

1435
01:08:40,199 --> 01:08:45,329
I read a sentence from a hiking guidebook.

1436
01:08:45,412 --> 01:08:51,794
People are worn out by modern society,
and their hidden…

1437
01:08:51,877 --> 01:08:53,295
People's…

1438
01:08:53,379 --> 01:08:54,797
That…

1439
01:08:54,880 --> 01:08:56,340
Beast?

1440
01:08:56,423 --> 01:08:57,299
Barbaric?

1441
01:08:57,383 --> 01:08:58,717
It's not barbaric.

1442
01:08:58,801 --> 01:09:00,052
It's…

1443
01:09:01,137 --> 01:09:03,889
What is it? Wild?

1444
01:09:03,973 --> 01:09:05,266
THE ANSWER IS "WILD NATURE"

1445
01:09:05,349 --> 01:09:08,811
<i>"It's an activity that awakens</i>

1446
01:09:08,894 --> 01:09:11,856
<i>the instinctive senses" is what it said.</i>

1447
01:09:11,939 --> 01:09:13,732
I don't understand what it means.

1448
01:09:15,860 --> 01:09:17,486
Rather, I've become

1449
01:09:18,529 --> 01:09:19,905
even more worn out.

1450
01:09:19,989 --> 01:09:21,574
I feel tired.

1451
01:09:22,658 --> 01:09:25,786
I FEEL TIRED

1452
01:09:33,544 --> 01:09:34,670
THE FOOD BREAKS THE SILENCE

1453
01:09:34,753 --> 01:09:36,338
-I'll grill this time.
-No.

1454
01:09:36,839 --> 01:09:40,050
WHEN YOU FEEL DOWN, EAT MEAT

1455
01:09:41,218 --> 01:09:46,515
THE FIRST MEAL AFTER DESCENDING
IS BEEF RIBS

1456
01:09:46,599 --> 01:09:50,019
WITH TOP 2 JJIGAES,
DOENJANG JJIGAE AND KIMCHI JJIGAE

1457
01:10:05,868 --> 01:10:11,916
THE TABLE IS DEAD SILENT

1458
01:10:15,419 --> 01:10:17,004
We have no energy at all,

1459
01:10:17,630 --> 01:10:19,089
so we can't talk.

1460
01:10:19,590 --> 01:10:20,841
I can't say anything.

1461
01:10:22,343 --> 01:10:24,178
But I can still eat meat.

1462
01:10:25,638 --> 01:10:28,140
Earlier, we ate at a very cold place.

1463
01:10:30,017 --> 01:10:32,269
Right, you need to decide the club name.

1464
01:10:34,605 --> 01:10:35,522
The hiking club name?

1465
01:10:36,565 --> 01:10:37,399
Descend?

1466
01:10:38,025 --> 01:10:39,610
-Descend?
-Descend.

1467
01:10:39,693 --> 01:10:40,611
That's good.

1468
01:10:41,153 --> 01:10:42,696
-Descend.
-Descend Club.

1469
01:10:42,780 --> 01:10:43,614
Descend.

1470
01:10:43,697 --> 01:10:44,990
-Why?
-I don't know.

1471
01:10:45,074 --> 01:10:46,450
Descending is nice.

1472
01:10:47,159 --> 01:10:48,953
I asked why you hiked,
and it's to descend?

1473
01:10:49,036 --> 01:10:50,788
THE ANSWER TO THE QUESTION: TO DESCEND

1474
01:10:50,871 --> 01:10:51,705
To descend.

1475
01:10:51,789 --> 01:10:54,041
Is it Descend Club,
as in our lives are going downhill?

1476
01:10:54,708 --> 01:10:56,043
That works too.

1477
01:10:56,126 --> 01:10:57,795
SATISFIED WITH THE DOUBLE MEANING

1478
01:10:57,878 --> 01:10:58,921
I like Descend Club.

1479
01:10:59,004 --> 01:11:00,172
THE CREATOR IS SATISFIED TOO

1480
01:11:00,256 --> 01:11:01,924
It looks very weak and nice.

1481
01:11:02,007 --> 01:11:03,968
HE IS VERY SELF-AWARE

1482
01:11:04,051 --> 01:11:06,845
DESCEND CLUB FORMED

1483
01:11:06,929 --> 01:11:07,972
Okay, then.

1484
01:11:08,055 --> 01:11:13,102
Today was Descend Club's training camp
and endurance test.

1485
01:11:13,602 --> 01:11:15,354
All four of you

1486
01:11:15,437 --> 01:11:16,272
have passed.

1487
01:11:16,355 --> 01:11:17,189
EVERYONE PASSES

1488
01:11:17,273 --> 01:11:20,067
CONGRATULATIONS, DESCEND CLUB

1489
01:11:24,989 --> 01:11:25,906
THE FIRST QUEST REVEAL

1490
01:11:25,990 --> 01:11:28,867
The first quest will unlock now.

1491
01:11:28,951 --> 01:11:31,954
Your first quest is…

1492
01:11:33,580 --> 01:11:34,623
this.

1493
01:11:34,707 --> 01:11:35,541
What?

1494
01:11:37,876 --> 01:11:38,877
This.

1495
01:11:39,378 --> 01:11:40,212
What?

1496
01:11:42,172 --> 01:11:47,636
37 HOURS LATER

1497
01:11:47,720 --> 01:11:49,888
My hands are freezing.

1498
01:11:49,972 --> 01:11:51,557
My hands are so cold.

1499
01:11:53,017 --> 01:11:54,101
<i>There's no shelter?</i>

1500
01:11:54,727 --> 01:11:56,061
<i>This is…</i>

1501
01:11:56,145 --> 01:11:57,271
Forget about the quest.

1502
01:11:57,354 --> 01:11:59,231
I actually kind of gave up.

1503
01:11:59,982 --> 01:12:01,400
Let's just go. Are you okay?

1504
01:12:01,483 --> 01:12:03,319
IT WILL DRIVE DESCEND CLUB INTO PANIC

1505
01:12:03,402 --> 01:12:05,237
I felt a bit anxious.

1506
01:12:05,321 --> 01:12:06,238
This…

1507
01:12:07,531 --> 01:12:08,991
All right, guys. Let's do this.

1508
01:12:09,074 --> 01:12:11,744
DESCEND CLUB'S FIRST QUEST

1509
01:12:11,827 --> 01:12:14,330
<i>I was on edge. We made it this far.</i>

1510
01:12:14,913 --> 01:12:16,623
If we fail…

1511
01:12:19,752 --> 01:12:21,211
-I…
-Yes?

1512
01:12:21,295 --> 01:12:23,714
I really can't do this show. Seriously.

1513
01:12:24,840 --> 01:12:26,300
-Car-the.
-Goodness.

1514
01:12:26,383 --> 01:12:27,217
Car-the.

1515
01:13:14,848 --> 01:13:16,850
Subtitle translation by: Kim Yeeun
